1
00:00:39,352 --> 00:00:47,352
(MELANCHOLIC MUSIC)

2
00:00:55,911 --> 00:01:03,911
(FAINT VOICES)

3
00:01:04,586 --> 00:01:12,260
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

4
00:01:12,302 --> 00:01:14,596
(TRADITIONAL MUSIC)

5
00:01:14,638 --> 00:01:22,354
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

6
00:01:22,395 --> 00:01:24,314
(FAINT VOICES)

7
00:01:25,816 --> 00:01:30,529
(THE GIRL AND HER
GRANDFATHER SPEAK IN ARABIC)

8
00:01:30,570 --> 00:01:38,570
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

9
00:01:42,165 --> 00:01:46,503
(THE GIRL SPEAKS IN ARABIC)

10
00:01:46,545 --> 00:01:48,755
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

11
00:01:48,797 --> 00:01:50,882
(FAINT VOICES)

12
00:01:50,924 --> 00:01:58,924
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

13
00:02:05,105 --> 00:02:13,105
(MELANCHOLIC MUSIC)

14
00:02:24,249 --> 00:02:27,169
(UNINTELLIGIBLE VOICES
FROM THE MOBILE HOME)

15
00:02:27,210 --> 00:02:29,129
(MELANCHOLIC MUSIC)

16
00:02:29,171 --> 00:02:30,964
(A DOOR OPENS)

17
00:02:31,715 --> 00:02:34,676
(AMINA LAUGHS AND MARA YAWNS)

18
00:02:34,718 --> 00:02:38,847
Hey, sweetie. Come here right now.

19
00:02:38,889 --> 00:02:40,849
(AMINA LAUGHS WITH JOY)

20
00:02:40,891 --> 00:02:44,978
- (Mara) So fancy for breakfast.
- (Joe) Amina, breakfast!

21
00:02:45,854 --> 00:02:48,023
(Amina) Grandpa!

22
00:02:48,064 --> 00:02:49,191
(COUGHS FROM THE KITCHEN)

23
00:02:49,232 --> 00:02:51,776
(MUSIC OF "LET ME BE YOUR WHISKEY"
BY ALEXANDER LUDWIG)

24
00:02:51,818 --> 00:02:55,989
(JOE IS COUGHING)

25
00:02:57,240 --> 00:03:00,785
- Hey. Morning, dad.
- (singing) <i>..the rain...</i>

26
00:03:02,162 --> 00:03:07,709
(singing together) <i>Let me be
your whiskey. Kill the pain.</i>

27
00:03:07,751 --> 00:03:10,503
Thank you.
(JOE MAKES A SOUND OF PAIN)

28
00:03:10,545 --> 00:03:13,173
- Oh, be careful.
- Yeah, yeah.

29
00:03:14,341 --> 00:03:16,885
Oh, you reunited with your best friend.

30
00:03:17,844 --> 00:03:24,142
Oh... If she sets her mind in something...
Reminds me someone I know.

31
00:03:25,644 --> 00:03:28,605
I don't know who that is.

32
00:03:28,647 --> 00:03:30,190
(Mara) Adorable.

33
00:03:30,232 --> 00:03:31,983
Mina, do you want orange juice?

34
00:03:32,025 --> 00:03:34,069
(CAR HONKING)
Daddy!

35
00:03:36,238 --> 00:03:39,324
- (Joe) I thought he was coming tomorrow.
- What date is it?

36
00:03:41,493 --> 00:03:43,536
Jesus, it's the 23rd.

37
00:03:43,578 --> 00:03:45,372
Shit!

38
00:03:49,042 --> 00:03:50,502
(BIRDS SINGING)

39
00:03:50,543 --> 00:03:53,213
(Mara) So, I conveniently forgot, sue me.

40
00:03:54,130 --> 00:03:56,591
(Joe) You can't stop her seeing her father.

41
00:03:56,633 --> 00:03:59,552
(MELANCHOLIC MUSIC)

42
00:03:59,594 --> 00:04:02,764
- You're taking his side now?
- It's not about sides.

43
00:04:02,806 --> 00:04:05,267
Your daughter deserves
to know her daddy.

44
00:04:05,308 --> 00:04:07,602
(MELANCHOLIC MUSIC)

45
00:04:07,644 --> 00:04:09,604
You know you loved each other once.

46
00:04:10,438 --> 00:04:12,399
(Mara) Yeah, I wasn't
the one who ruined it.

47
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:16,194
(Mara) He was working late hours,
doing God knows what with who.

48
00:04:17,445 --> 00:04:19,072
I know.

49
00:04:19,114 --> 00:04:21,866
(MELANCHOLIC MUSIC)

50
00:04:21,908 --> 00:04:24,244
Come here right now.

51
00:04:24,286 --> 00:04:27,247
(MELANCHOLIC MUSIC)

52
00:04:27,289 --> 00:04:35,046
(AMINA SCREAMS WITH JOY AND LAUGHS)

53
00:04:35,088 --> 00:04:42,554
(MELANCHOLIC MUSIC)

54
00:04:42,595 --> 00:04:45,849
There's daddy. Okay, all right.

55
00:04:47,142 --> 00:04:48,435
(Amina) Daddy!

56
00:04:48,476 --> 00:04:50,687
(Karim) Hello, puppy.

57
00:04:50,729 --> 00:04:53,606
(KARIM LAUGHS JOYFULLY)

58
00:04:53,648 --> 00:04:58,028
(UNINTELLIGIBLE VOICES FROM KARIM)

59
00:05:00,113 --> 00:05:02,532
10:00 am, as promised.

60
00:05:02,574 --> 00:05:06,369
- I'll bring her back at 6:00.
- Okay. Bye, baby.

61
00:05:06,411 --> 00:05:07,954
(SMACKING KISSES)

62
00:05:10,832 --> 00:05:14,294
Are you okay?
You seem a little distracted.

63
00:05:14,336 --> 00:05:18,381
Uhm... Yeah, yeah,
I'm fine. Just work stuff.

64
00:05:18,423 --> 00:05:19,966
(Karim) I'm good.

65
00:05:20,675 --> 00:05:21,968
Okay.

66
00:05:26,014 --> 00:05:27,766
(Karim) Watch your hands, Amina.

67
00:05:37,108 --> 00:05:39,778
(Mara) Hey, what you got there?

68
00:05:40,862 --> 00:05:42,655
(Mara) What's this?

69
00:05:48,036 --> 00:05:51,915
(Mara) Should we have a story?
You want a story? Yeah.

70
00:05:51,956 --> 00:05:59,214
(MELANCHOLIC MUSIC)

71
00:05:59,255 --> 00:06:01,716
(Mara) Riky and Raky's adventure
began at the zoo.

72
00:06:01,758 --> 00:06:03,885
(Amina) Dinosaurs live in the zoo!

73
00:06:03,927 --> 00:06:06,888
- (Mara) In our story, they do.
- (Amina) Yes!

74
00:06:06,930 --> 00:06:14,930
(MELANCHOLIC MUSIC)

75
00:06:24,531 --> 00:06:27,450
- (Mara) Do you like your new costume?
- Yes, Mama!

76
00:06:27,492 --> 00:06:28,827
Yes!

77
00:06:28,868 --> 00:06:31,830
(Mara) Now, what are we missing?

78
00:06:31,871 --> 00:06:34,332
(Mara) Drugs! For papa, of course.

79
00:06:34,374 --> 00:06:36,167
(MARA AND AMINA LAUGH)

80
00:06:36,209 --> 00:06:39,504
- (Mara) That's not what we pay.
- But it is what your father's medication costs.

81
00:06:39,546 --> 00:06:43,174
That may be. But I've never paid
that before. I have all the records here.

82
00:06:45,844 --> 00:06:48,304
<i>(from the loudspeaker) Today's</i>
special discount...

83
00:06:48,346 --> 00:06:53,143
<i>...customers can get 20% off,</i>
please take your coupon to the checkout.

84
00:06:54,102 --> 00:06:57,123
- (Mara) Can I just see the manager?
- (Pharmacy manager) I am the manager, Ma'am.

85
00:06:57,147 --> 00:06:58,940
(Mara) What happened to Frank?

86
00:06:58,982 --> 00:07:02,485
(Pharmacy manager) He retired last week.
Moved to Boca with his family.

87
00:07:03,403 --> 00:07:05,684
- (Pharmacy manager) Just give me a minute.
- (Mara) Yeah.

88
00:07:20,003 --> 00:07:23,381
Oh! Okay, I think I see what's going on.

89
00:07:23,423 --> 00:07:27,385
(Pharmacy manager) You are right.
We just update some details.

90
00:07:29,596 --> 00:07:31,097
I'm so sorry about that, Ma'am.

91
00:07:31,139 --> 00:07:33,600
- You can go and pay at the cashier up front.
- Thank you.

92
00:07:39,731 --> 00:07:41,232
Mina?

93
00:07:43,985 --> 00:07:47,322
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

94
00:07:47,363 --> 00:07:49,073
(Mara) Amina?

95
00:07:49,115 --> 00:07:51,993
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

96
00:07:52,035 --> 00:07:53,703
(Mara) Mina?

97
00:07:53,745 --> 00:07:55,288
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

98
00:07:55,330 --> 00:07:56,956
Amina?!

99
00:07:56,998 --> 00:07:59,501
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

100
00:07:59,542 --> 00:08:01,419
MINA!

101
00:08:02,962 --> 00:08:05,798
Has anyone seen my daughter?
She's dressed as a dinosaur...

102
00:08:05,840 --> 00:08:08,194
(Security guard, muffled voice) Ma'am,
I need you to step outside the store...

103
00:08:08,218 --> 00:08:11,596
(muffled voice) Have you seen her?
Is she here? Fuck!

104
00:08:12,639 --> 00:08:18,853
Mina! Have you seen a little girl? She's
only four! Please, God, please, help me!

105
00:08:19,854 --> 00:08:24,567
(Mara, crying) Oh, my God! Please!

106
00:08:25,818 --> 00:08:32,075
(MARA CRIES OUT LOUD)

107
00:08:32,116 --> 00:08:39,874
(DRAMATIC MUSIC)

108
00:08:39,916 --> 00:08:44,504
- Did you find them? Where are they?
- Give them a chance. What's going on?

109
00:08:47,382 --> 00:08:49,342
We're doing everything
we can to find Amina.

110
00:08:49,384 --> 00:08:51,636
I know Karim took her.

111
00:08:53,304 --> 00:08:58,142
I know he did.
He was acting real fucking weird yesterday.

112
00:08:59,894 --> 00:09:02,814
And then Mina told me he was
talking about me to someone on the phone.

113
00:09:02,855 --> 00:09:04,524
- He's threatened it before.
- He has.

114
00:09:04,566 --> 00:09:07,193
If that's the case,
we're struggling to understand...

115
00:09:07,235 --> 00:09:10,697
...why Karim didn't just keep Amina
on one of his visits.

116
00:09:10,738 --> 00:09:12,615
How am I supposed to know that?

117
00:09:12,657 --> 00:09:14,951
Can you think of anything
you may have done?

118
00:09:16,160 --> 00:09:19,163
- Something I may have done?
- Goddamn' it. This ain't her fault.

119
00:09:19,205 --> 00:09:20,641
(Male detective) I didn't mean that.

120
00:09:20,665 --> 00:09:23,710
She didn't do anything to cause this.
What the fuck is wrong with you?

121
00:09:23,751 --> 00:09:26,796
(MARA CRIES)

122
00:09:28,089 --> 00:09:30,675
I think he's gonna take her home.

123
00:09:33,011 --> 00:09:34,304
Home?

124
00:09:34,345 --> 00:09:36,889
- Syria.
- (Joe) Syria.

125
00:09:36,931 --> 00:09:39,225
He used to talk about it all the time.

126
00:09:40,018 --> 00:09:43,479
(Mara) Getting a job
at a hospital near his family.

127
00:09:43,521 --> 00:09:46,065
(Mara) We got divorced,
he tried to do it then,

128
00:09:46,107 --> 00:09:49,569
I had to get a restraining order,
to stop him taking her out of the country.

129
00:09:49,611 --> 00:09:51,988
You need to check all the airports.

130
00:09:57,243 --> 00:09:59,245
What? What is it?

131
00:10:01,372 --> 00:10:04,292
There isn't a federal law that
prevents a parent taking their child...

132
00:10:04,334 --> 00:10:06,628
It's kidnapping. He's kidnapped her.

133
00:10:06,669 --> 00:10:09,172
...their own child internationally.

134
00:10:10,256 --> 00:10:13,152
(Female detective) If that's the case,
I'm sorry, there's nothing we can do.

135
00:10:13,176 --> 00:10:17,764
You've gotta be kidding?
He can just... He can just take her?

136
00:10:19,307 --> 00:10:22,435
So I just... I just...
I lose my daughter?

137
00:10:22,477 --> 00:10:24,646
(Male detective) We're following
all the procedures...

138
00:10:24,687 --> 00:10:27,482
...we have roadblocks in places...

139
00:10:27,523 --> 00:10:30,818
(THE VOICE DISSOLVES)

140
00:10:30,860 --> 00:10:33,571
What other possibilities? What?

141
00:10:37,367 --> 00:10:39,661
You mean like a child-snatcher?

142
00:10:41,371 --> 00:10:45,124
Yes, could you tell me which Ohio airport
I'd need for a flight to Syria?

143
00:10:45,166 --> 00:10:47,752
<i>- (Female operator) Hold, please.</i>
- (Mara) Ah-ah.

144
00:10:47,794 --> 00:10:55,259
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

145
00:10:55,301 --> 00:10:58,930
<i>(Mara) You can't hide from me. I see you.</i>

146
00:10:58,971 --> 00:11:00,890
<i>- (Amina) Ah!</i>
- (Mara) There she is!

147
00:11:00,932 --> 00:11:04,936
<i>(Female operator) Flights to Syria depart</i>
from Port Columbus via Amsterdam

148
00:11:04,977 --> 00:11:08,022
<i>and rage from $750 to $1000.</i>

149
00:11:08,731 --> 00:11:10,316
(Mara) Okay, thank you.

150
00:11:10,358 --> 00:11:14,696
We went to Karim's house.
I'm afraid it was cleared out.

151
00:11:16,155 --> 00:11:18,324
(Male detective) There were
just a few things left.

152
00:11:25,832 --> 00:11:28,000
Did you check Port Columbus airport?

153
00:11:28,835 --> 00:11:31,379
We found his car in long-term storage.

154
00:11:32,755 --> 00:11:36,759
(Male detective) We're checking flight lists,
but we now suspect he has left the country.

155
00:11:40,805 --> 00:11:48,688
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

156
00:11:48,730 --> 00:11:51,357
(Mara) Karim Saleh Taleb.

157
00:11:51,399 --> 00:11:53,860
(Joe) She doesn't have
any contacts for his family.

158
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:57,113
- (Mara) Radiology.
<i>- (Female operator) Sorry, I don't understand.</i>

159
00:11:58,489 --> 00:12:03,703
He said his father lived in Riyadh, in Saudi
Arabia, but there's no record of him being there.

160
00:12:07,874 --> 00:12:11,419
(Joe) Look, she never went there
and they never came here!

161
00:12:11,461 --> 00:12:14,213
<i>(Female operator) Sorry,</i>
I don't have anyone by that name.

162
00:12:14,255 --> 00:12:15,965
- Okay.
- (Joe) I don't know.

163
00:12:16,007 --> 00:12:19,635
You're the lawyer, don't you
have an investigator or something?

164
00:12:19,677 --> 00:12:21,220
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

165
00:12:21,262 --> 00:12:23,556
(Joe) I don't like your
attitude either, pal!

166
00:12:23,598 --> 00:12:25,808
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

167
00:12:25,850 --> 00:12:27,435
(Joe) Oh, God...

168
00:12:27,477 --> 00:12:31,105
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

169
00:12:31,147 --> 00:12:33,733
(SOUND OF A GUN LOADING AND THEN A SHOT)

170
00:12:35,902 --> 00:12:37,862
(GUNSHOT)

171
00:12:38,946 --> 00:12:41,240
(GUNSHOT)

172
00:12:41,282 --> 00:12:43,201
(MUSIC FROM THE RADIO STOPS)

173
00:12:45,119 --> 00:12:47,830
(DOG BARKING OUTSIDE)

174
00:12:55,004 --> 00:13:03,004
(SAD MUSIC)

175
00:13:21,656 --> 00:13:23,533
(NON AUDIBLE CRYING)

176
00:13:23,574 --> 00:13:27,328
(SAD MUSIC)

177
00:13:27,370 --> 00:13:35,370
(MARA CRIES DESPERATELY)

178
00:13:37,046 --> 00:13:40,550
(SAD MUSIC)

179
00:13:40,591 --> 00:13:46,806
When Karim took Amina overseas,
it wasn't a crime, if you can believe that.

180
00:13:48,975 --> 00:13:51,894
I've been without my baby girl for...

181
00:13:53,479 --> 00:13:55,022
...(crying) over two years.

182
00:13:55,064 --> 00:13:57,400
(MELANCHOLIC MUSIC)

183
00:13:57,441 --> 00:14:00,570
And every day I don't get to see her...

184
00:14:02,446 --> 00:14:04,574
...it hurts like a bullet.

185
00:14:05,700 --> 00:14:09,287
Thanks to your incredible generosity...

186
00:14:10,246 --> 00:14:12,290
...I'm gonna get to go to Washington.

187
00:14:12,665 --> 00:14:16,460
And I'm gonna knock on every door
and talk to every suit.

188
00:14:16,502 --> 00:14:19,672
(Mara) And do everything
I can to find my baby.

189
00:14:19,714 --> 00:14:24,010
I won't rest until I bring her home,
where she belongs.

190
00:14:24,051 --> 00:14:28,556
(Mara) My mum left me when I was little,
I am not walking away from my own.

191
00:14:28,598 --> 00:14:36,598
(PEOPLE CLAP AND CHEER MARA)

192
00:14:37,690 --> 00:14:41,152
(MELANCHOLIC MUSIC)

193
00:14:41,193 --> 00:14:43,362
(DOG WHINING)

194
00:14:44,822 --> 00:14:46,532
(JOE COUGHS)

195
00:14:46,574 --> 00:14:50,578
- I'm afraid to leave you.
- (coughing) No, stop right there.

196
00:14:52,872 --> 00:14:57,501
You stick to your guns.
Just like I taught you. Yeah.

197
00:14:58,586 --> 00:15:02,548
(JOE INHALES AND EXHALES DEEPLY)

198
00:15:02,590 --> 00:15:04,759
- I love you.
- I love you.

199
00:15:05,968 --> 00:15:09,096
(MARA SNIFFLES)

200
00:15:09,138 --> 00:15:17,138
(EPIC MUSIC)

201
00:15:18,773 --> 00:15:21,984
(FAINT VOICES)

202
00:15:22,026 --> 00:15:23,235
Take it.

203
00:15:23,277 --> 00:15:26,697
- State your intent.
- (Mara) Petition for a Senate resolution.

204
00:15:26,739 --> 00:15:30,409
And the support of your governor,
then bring it back.

205
00:15:30,451 --> 00:15:32,036
You can't block the door, Ma'am.

206
00:15:32,078 --> 00:15:34,222
Excuse me, I can stand here,
it's my First Amendment right!

207
00:15:34,246 --> 00:15:36,916
An appointment will be sent to you
within the next six months.

208
00:15:36,958 --> 00:15:39,168
Six months? I think I'll wait.

209
00:15:39,710 --> 00:15:41,462
Ma'am...

210
00:15:41,504 --> 00:15:44,674
(MELANCHOLIC MUSIC)

211
00:15:44,715 --> 00:15:49,345
Do you speak English?
I can't read the signature on my x-ray.

212
00:15:50,054 --> 00:15:54,642
The majority of kidnappings
in this country are committed by parents.

213
00:15:54,684 --> 00:15:57,979
I think it says Karim Taleb.

214
00:15:58,020 --> 00:16:04,902
Last year, over 25 thousand children were
abducted by parents and nothing is being done!

215
00:16:04,944 --> 00:16:07,697
<i>(Female operator) There's no position here</i>
by that name.

216
00:16:07,738 --> 00:16:10,241
Okay. Thanks anyway.

217
00:16:10,282 --> 00:16:15,621
(MELANCHOLIC MUSIC)

218
00:16:15,663 --> 00:16:19,375
<i>(ANCHORMAN, ON TV) Mara Danning has returned</i>
to Washington to action a hunger strike...

219
00:16:19,417 --> 00:16:21,585
<i>...with the parent's
protest group she formed...</i>

220
00:16:21,627 --> 00:16:25,214
<i>...in the wake of the disappearance</i>
of her daughter, four years ago.

221
00:16:25,256 --> 00:16:29,427
(MELANCHOLIC MUSIC)

222
00:16:29,468 --> 00:16:37,468
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

223
00:16:46,819 --> 00:16:54,819
(WIND BLOWING)

224
00:16:59,832 --> 00:17:07,832
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

225
00:17:27,610 --> 00:17:29,195
(Robeson) Mind if I sit?

226
00:17:30,738 --> 00:17:32,656
(MARA SIGHS)

227
00:17:32,698 --> 00:17:35,785
- Can I help you with something?
- (Robeson) No.

228
00:17:36,368 --> 00:17:38,329
(Robeson) But I might be able to help you.

229
00:17:40,581 --> 00:17:43,709
Look, cowboy,
I just want to be alone, okay?

230
00:17:55,471 --> 00:17:57,640
(Robeson) I'm in the
child recovery business.

231
00:18:06,440 --> 00:18:14,440
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

232
00:18:15,032 --> 00:18:16,325
You did this?

233
00:18:16,367 --> 00:18:19,912
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

234
00:18:19,954 --> 00:18:21,122
Is it legal?

235
00:18:22,790 --> 00:18:24,500
As legal as abduction.

236
00:18:24,542 --> 00:18:27,378
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

237
00:18:27,419 --> 00:18:28,921
I'm broke, so...

238
00:18:28,963 --> 00:18:30,506
I know.

239
00:18:30,548 --> 00:18:32,174
Keep that.

240
00:18:33,050 --> 00:18:35,469
(Robeson) I have a proposition for you.

241
00:18:35,511 --> 00:18:37,263
Come work for me.

242
00:18:37,304 --> 00:18:39,223
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

243
00:18:39,265 --> 00:18:41,892
(Robeson) You help me
find other people's kids.

244
00:18:41,934 --> 00:18:44,270
I'll help you find yours.

245
00:18:44,311 --> 00:18:46,689
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

246
00:18:46,730 --> 00:18:50,776
You know, it pays pretty good too.

247
00:18:50,818 --> 00:18:54,363
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

248
00:18:54,405 --> 00:18:56,240
(Robeson) Call me.

249
00:18:56,282 --> 00:19:04,282
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

250
00:19:13,716 --> 00:19:17,344
Mara, this is Carl. Heads up linguistics,
pretty much anything I can't do.

251
00:19:17,386 --> 00:19:19,221
He's my second-in-command.

252
00:19:19,263 --> 00:19:21,599
- I'm your only-in-command...
- (Robeson) Right.

253
00:19:22,183 --> 00:19:24,602
- Nice to meet you.
- Glad you called.

254
00:19:24,643 --> 00:19:26,437
It's not a yes.

255
00:19:27,771 --> 00:19:29,273
Okay.

256
00:19:29,773 --> 00:19:31,275
It's for you.

257
00:19:34,570 --> 00:19:39,033
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

258
00:19:49,835 --> 00:19:52,254
Hey. This is a good thing.

259
00:19:52,296 --> 00:19:56,592
(Robeson) I have contacts all over
the Middle East. We'll find her. In time.

260
00:19:56,634 --> 00:20:01,847
(Mara) I haven't seen my daughter
in four years, 86 days, four hours...

261
00:20:02,598 --> 00:20:05,768
- (Carl) How long has it been since you've eaten?
- (Mara) Nine days.

262
00:20:06,518 --> 00:20:07,937
(Carl) Here.

263
00:20:09,730 --> 00:20:11,398
(Mara) I can't.

264
00:20:14,318 --> 00:20:16,779
(Robeson) We're your best option, Mara.

265
00:20:30,084 --> 00:20:33,170
(MARA COUGHS AND THEN THROWS UP)

266
00:20:33,212 --> 00:20:34,797
(Carl) You alright?

267
00:20:35,506 --> 00:20:37,091
(Robeson) Here.

268
00:20:40,469 --> 00:20:44,890
(Mara) I don't understand why you want me.
I trained as a seamstress.

269
00:20:44,932 --> 00:20:48,269
(Robeson) Well, if I can
be completely honest...

270
00:20:48,310 --> 00:20:50,104
...we need a woman in our team.

271
00:20:50,145 --> 00:20:52,398
(Robeson) You rouse less suspicion
in this line of work.

272
00:20:52,439 --> 00:20:54,233
(Carl) And you're tough.

273
00:20:57,111 --> 00:20:58,904
(Robeson) That should get you started.

274
00:21:00,864 --> 00:21:03,200
Enough to help with your dad's treatments.

275
00:21:08,747 --> 00:21:11,792
Are you ready for your first case?
Come with me.

276
00:21:11,834 --> 00:21:18,841
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

277
00:21:18,882 --> 00:21:21,260
(Robeson) This... This is Maya.

278
00:21:21,302 --> 00:21:24,096
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

279
00:21:24,138 --> 00:21:26,390
That's her son, JD.

280
00:21:27,808 --> 00:21:33,355
(Robeson) Barely sees the father until one day
he decides: "You know what? I want my kid back".

281
00:21:33,397 --> 00:21:37,234
(Robeson) He beats her senseless
and then takes the kid back to Mexico.

282
00:21:38,652 --> 00:21:41,989
(Robeson) I need more
intel. She's holding back.

283
00:21:42,740 --> 00:21:44,783
Figure she's scared.

284
00:21:44,825 --> 00:21:49,621
Well, of course she's scared. Look at
you. You're like a goddamn sack of rocks.

285
00:21:49,663 --> 00:21:53,334
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

286
00:21:53,375 --> 00:21:56,712
No one knows what this feels like
more than you, Mara.

287
00:21:56,754 --> 00:22:04,754
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

288
00:22:09,058 --> 00:22:13,520
He said you could get him back. Is it true?

289
00:22:14,980 --> 00:22:19,026
Please. I just want him with me.

290
00:22:19,068 --> 00:22:22,696
(crying) I can't sleep. I can't breathe.

291
00:22:23,447 --> 00:22:26,158
We will try to get him back.

292
00:22:26,200 --> 00:22:29,787
First, could you just tell me
a little bit about your son?

293
00:22:30,204 --> 00:22:31,789
(MAYA SIGHS)

294
00:22:31,830 --> 00:22:35,626
He is gentle, you know.

295
00:22:35,667 --> 00:22:40,589
He can spend hours drawing and...

296
00:22:40,631 --> 00:22:42,633
(MAYA SIGHS)

297
00:22:42,674 --> 00:22:44,551
...he really likes animals.

298
00:22:44,593 --> 00:22:52,593
(MELANCHOLIC MUSIC)

299
00:22:56,063 --> 00:23:00,025
- What part do I play?
- Your job is to keep the child calm.

300
00:23:00,067 --> 00:23:02,379
(Robeson) At least until we can hand him
back to the client.

301
00:23:02,403 --> 00:23:05,406
You give us plausibility,
keep everything looking normal.

302
00:23:06,156 --> 00:23:08,534
- So I'm playing mother.
- (Robeson) Exactly.

303
00:23:08,575 --> 00:23:11,453
Let me run you through
the plan, step by step.

304
00:23:12,788 --> 00:23:18,752
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

305
00:23:18,794 --> 00:23:21,130
(Robeson) Finding and recovering
the target is hard enough.

306
00:23:21,171 --> 00:23:23,715
Then you get him across
the border with fake paperwork.

307
00:23:23,757 --> 00:23:26,969
- How do we do that?
- This is only Mexico to Arizona. It's easy.

308
00:23:27,010 --> 00:23:33,267
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

309
00:23:33,308 --> 00:23:39,815
(TOLLING BELLS)

310
00:23:39,857 --> 00:23:41,942
(Robeson) A lot of stray dogs in Mexico.

311
00:23:41,984 --> 00:23:49,984
(TOLLING BELLS)

312
00:23:55,205 --> 00:23:57,875
(FAINT VOICES)

313
00:24:01,086 --> 00:24:09,086
(FAINT VOICES)

314
00:24:10,929 --> 00:24:16,393
(CHILDREN CRYING)

315
00:24:20,022 --> 00:24:25,235
(FAINT VOICES)

316
00:24:25,277 --> 00:24:33,277
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

317
00:24:38,415 --> 00:24:39,917
Hey...

318
00:24:39,958 --> 00:24:44,838
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

319
00:24:51,803 --> 00:24:59,803
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

320
00:25:03,106 --> 00:25:06,276
(UNINTELLIGIBLE DIALOGUE)

321
00:25:06,318 --> 00:25:08,237
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

322
00:25:08,278 --> 00:25:10,697
(Robeson) Okay, we're on. Let's go.

323
00:25:10,739 --> 00:25:18,739
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

324
00:25:26,797 --> 00:25:28,507
Keep a lookout.

325
00:25:28,549 --> 00:25:36,549
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

326
00:25:38,475 --> 00:25:39,851
Shit...

327
00:25:39,893 --> 00:25:44,856
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

328
00:25:44,898 --> 00:25:46,483
We're in.

329
00:25:46,525 --> 00:25:54,074
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

330
00:25:54,116 --> 00:25:57,119
Oh, oh. Hey, wait.

331
00:25:57,160 --> 00:26:05,160
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

332
00:26:05,586 --> 00:26:07,588
- Shit!
- What?

333
00:26:07,629 --> 00:26:09,172
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

334
00:26:09,214 --> 00:26:11,508
Class must have cancelled. Move it.

335
00:26:11,550 --> 00:26:15,429
(FAINT VOICES)

336
00:26:15,470 --> 00:26:17,431
(Carl) Damn! We missed our window.

337
00:26:20,684 --> 00:26:22,686
(Robeson) Means we're
going to have to improvise.

338
00:26:24,062 --> 00:26:26,773
(DOG BARKING)

339
00:26:26,815 --> 00:26:33,113
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

340
00:26:33,155 --> 00:26:36,575
- Hey, get ready.
- We can't do it here, can we?

341
00:26:36,617 --> 00:26:44,617
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

342
00:26:49,838 --> 00:26:51,882
(DOG BARKING)

343
00:26:51,923 --> 00:26:54,968
(FAINT VOICES)

344
00:26:55,010 --> 00:26:56,428
(Carl) Hey.

345
00:26:56,470 --> 00:27:01,850
(FAINT VOICES)

346
00:27:01,892 --> 00:27:03,602
(DOG BARKING)

347
00:27:03,644 --> 00:27:05,437
(Carl) Wanna play with her?

348
00:27:05,479 --> 00:27:07,814
(FAINT VOICES)

349
00:27:07,856 --> 00:27:10,150
(ROBESON WHISTLES)
(Carl) What is that?

350
00:27:10,192 --> 00:27:15,947
(DOG BARKING AND JD LAUGHING)

351
00:27:15,989 --> 00:27:18,325
(JD) Oh! No, no!

352
00:27:18,367 --> 00:27:20,511
(Robeson) Take him! Take him!
(UNINTELLIGIBLE WORDS BY JD)

353
00:27:20,535 --> 00:27:23,705
(Robeson) Take him! Take him!
(UNINTELLIGIBLE WORDS BY JD)

354
00:27:23,747 --> 00:27:28,085
(UNINTELLIGIBLE WORDS BY JD, MARA SIGHS)

355
00:27:28,126 --> 00:27:34,299
(SUSPENSE MUSIC AND CRYING)

356
00:27:34,341 --> 00:27:36,927
You do it! Go, Go!

357
00:27:36,968 --> 00:27:39,888
(UNINTELLIGIBLE WORDS BY JD)
(Robeson) Come on, go! Go!

358
00:27:39,930 --> 00:27:42,516
Come with me, it's okay! Come on!

359
00:27:46,228 --> 00:27:50,315
(Carl) Hey. What the fuck you looking at?
Get out of here.

360
00:27:50,357 --> 00:27:52,484
(FIGHTING SOUNDS)

361
00:27:53,777 --> 00:27:56,363
I'm not going to hurt you, okay?

362
00:27:56,405 --> 00:28:00,826
I'm taking you home to see your mom.
Mama. Would you like that?

363
00:28:00,867 --> 00:28:03,120
Good boy. Hold my hand.

364
00:28:03,161 --> 00:28:07,749
(FIGHTING SOUNDS AND UNINTELLIGIBLE VOICES)

365
00:28:07,791 --> 00:28:14,840
(FIGHTING SOUNDS AND SCREAMS)

366
00:28:14,881 --> 00:28:22,881
(FIGHTING SOUNDS)

367
00:28:23,432 --> 00:28:26,518
(ROBESON SCREAMS WITH PAIN)
Shit!

368
00:28:26,560 --> 00:28:34,560
(AGITATED MUSIC)

369
00:28:59,885 --> 00:29:02,345
(THE WOMAN SCREAMS)
(Mara) Oh, sorry!

370
00:29:02,387 --> 00:29:04,639
Mara! Mara. Hey.

371
00:29:05,724 --> 00:29:08,101
(THE WOMAN MAKES ANGRY SOUNDS)

372
00:29:08,143 --> 00:29:09,853
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

373
00:29:09,895 --> 00:29:11,897
(Robeson) This way. This way!

374
00:29:11,938 --> 00:29:13,648
(JD'S FATHER IS SPEAKING IN SPANISH)

375
00:29:13,690 --> 00:29:17,694
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

376
00:29:17,736 --> 00:29:21,782
(Carl) Here! Come on.
Move, move, move, come on!

377
00:29:21,823 --> 00:29:25,702
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

378
00:29:25,744 --> 00:29:28,205
(Robeson) Come on! Go, go, go!

379
00:29:28,246 --> 00:29:31,249
(TIRES SCREECHING)

380
00:29:31,291 --> 00:29:33,126
(JD'S FATHER IS SPEAKING IN SPANISH)

381
00:29:33,168 --> 00:29:35,337
(TIRES SCREECHING)

382
00:29:35,378 --> 00:29:37,923
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

383
00:29:37,964 --> 00:29:41,802
(MARA GASPS FOR BREATH)

384
00:29:41,843 --> 00:29:49,843
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

385
00:30:06,618 --> 00:30:08,703
Hey, we just...

386
00:30:10,497 --> 00:30:13,416
All right. Good boy.

387
00:30:14,501 --> 00:30:16,962
(SOUND OF A CAR APPROACHING)

388
00:30:17,003 --> 00:30:19,005
(Robeson) All right, she's here.

389
00:30:19,047 --> 00:30:21,675
Keep him here.
Once we're paid, we'll bring her in.

390
00:30:21,716 --> 00:30:24,052
Are you fucking serious?

391
00:30:24,094 --> 00:30:26,137
Business first.

392
00:30:28,014 --> 00:30:30,684
Two more minutes, I promise, alright?

393
00:30:30,725 --> 00:30:33,478
- (Maya) Thank you for your time.
- (Robeson) Of course.

394
00:30:33,520 --> 00:30:35,039
- (Maya) May I go?
- (Robeson) He is waiting for you.

395
00:30:35,063 --> 00:30:36,815
(Maya) Thank you.

396
00:30:38,108 --> 00:30:43,113
Oh, my God. Oh! Oh, my God!

397
00:30:43,154 --> 00:30:46,157
(Maya, crying) Oh, my God!

398
00:30:46,199 --> 00:30:48,159
(CHEERFUL MUSIC)

399
00:30:48,201 --> 00:30:51,454
(Maya, crying) Oh! Oh!

400
00:30:51,496 --> 00:30:54,457
(MAYA AND JD CRY)

401
00:30:54,499 --> 00:30:57,627
(MELANCHOLIC MUSIC)

402
00:30:57,669 --> 00:31:00,046
(Robeson) Can I have
what she's having, please?

403
00:31:01,047 --> 00:31:02,757
(Robeson) Hey.

404
00:31:03,508 --> 00:31:05,135
(Robeson) How you doing'?

405
00:31:07,679 --> 00:31:09,723
(ROBESON SIGHS WITH RELIEF)

406
00:31:09,764 --> 00:31:11,641
(Robeson) Your cut.

407
00:31:15,562 --> 00:31:19,441
- (Robeson) Thank you.
- Wow. That's...

408
00:31:19,482 --> 00:31:21,735
That's more than I make in six months.

409
00:31:21,776 --> 00:31:25,322
Oh, that's just a fraction
of what I need for Amina.

410
00:31:25,363 --> 00:31:28,658
We did something good here.
You know that, right?

411
00:31:28,700 --> 00:31:31,494
So how come I feel like a mercenary?

412
00:31:32,162 --> 00:31:34,706
We have to be paid
for the risks we take.

413
00:31:34,748 --> 00:31:36,499
She was desperate.

414
00:31:36,541 --> 00:31:41,004
(Robeson) But she found the money.
And that's good, right?

415
00:31:42,047 --> 00:31:43,798
I could never afford that.

416
00:31:43,840 --> 00:31:45,467
You won't have to.

417
00:31:47,135 --> 00:31:51,264
(Mara) Right. "Quid pro quo".
It's the jobs they'll pay for it.

418
00:31:51,306 --> 00:31:53,058
Eventually.

419
00:31:53,099 --> 00:31:54,893
How long's eventually?

420
00:31:54,935 --> 00:31:56,770
Sometimes it's cut and dry.

421
00:31:56,811 --> 00:32:00,190
You know, you find the kid, you find
a way in. It's pretty straightforward.

422
00:32:00,231 --> 00:32:03,360
But not mine, right? Not Amina.

423
00:32:03,985 --> 00:32:08,949
Well, your ex is pretty good
at covering his tracks, but you know that.

424
00:32:08,990 --> 00:32:12,035
(Robeson) I mean, you've been
looking for him a lot longer than I have.

425
00:32:13,370 --> 00:32:15,956
You don't have kids of your own, right?

426
00:32:15,997 --> 00:32:17,916
- (Robeson) No.
- So...

427
00:32:18,959 --> 00:32:20,794
Why do you do it?

428
00:32:20,835 --> 00:32:22,587
(ROBESON SIGHS)

429
00:32:23,129 --> 00:32:27,467
Well, I've just gotten out of the Marines.
Panama City Beach.

430
00:32:28,551 --> 00:32:33,139
Was pretty down and out.
Didn't have a lot of transferable skills.

431
00:32:33,181 --> 00:32:36,726
(Robeson) And I was hanging at the
vet center, you know, looking for work.

432
00:32:36,768 --> 00:32:39,688
(Robeson) Then one
day, this guy comes in...

433
00:32:39,729 --> 00:32:43,483
...and he's talking about this Washington
mom who wanted her kid snatched back.

434
00:32:43,525 --> 00:32:45,735
(Robeson) You know, it
was really good money.

435
00:32:45,777 --> 00:32:48,029
Turns out...

436
00:32:48,071 --> 00:32:52,158
I was pretty good at it.
You know, gave me purpose.

437
00:32:53,493 --> 00:32:56,705
So then I don't know,
formed the unit, hired Carl.

438
00:32:57,747 --> 00:32:59,708
Rest is history.

439
00:33:01,084 --> 00:33:03,336
You ever had a job go bad?

440
00:33:05,380 --> 00:33:09,801
Let's not dwell on that. Okay?
Today was a good day.

441
00:33:10,802 --> 00:33:12,929
To your future.

442
00:33:13,763 --> 00:33:17,308
(FAST-PACED MUSIC)

443
00:33:17,350 --> 00:33:18,685
(Carl) Scotland?

444
00:33:18,727 --> 00:33:21,455
(Robeson) The kid's grandmother gave
evidence that the stepfather is violent.

445
00:33:21,479 --> 00:33:23,398
Yeah, he has convictions...

446
00:33:23,440 --> 00:33:26,860
...but he won't be in Edinburgh when we
snatch back, he'll be traveling for work.

447
00:33:26,901 --> 00:33:34,901
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

448
00:33:38,163 --> 00:33:40,206
(AIRPORT OF PARIS-LE BOURGET)

449
00:33:40,248 --> 00:33:46,796
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

450
00:33:46,838 --> 00:33:48,423
Okay.

451
00:33:48,465 --> 00:33:56,465
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

452
00:34:07,275 --> 00:34:11,488
(MUSIC FADES)

453
00:34:14,657 --> 00:34:17,035
<i>- (Female operator) May I help you?</i>
- (Mara) Yeah. Hi.

454
00:34:17,077 --> 00:34:21,081
Could you tell me who I need to speak to
get a list of all the hospitals in Lebanon?

455
00:34:22,332 --> 00:34:25,168
We have a new case. Top priority.

456
00:34:26,795 --> 00:34:28,463
Albania!

457
00:34:28,922 --> 00:34:31,382
Thought it was getting
pretty rough out there. It's in chaos.

458
00:34:31,424 --> 00:34:33,802
Yeah, well, chaos is good cover.

459
00:34:36,763 --> 00:34:39,516
- Where's the rest of the intel?
- That's all I have.

460
00:34:39,557 --> 00:34:47,557
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

461
00:34:50,944 --> 00:34:58,944
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

462
00:35:03,998 --> 00:35:11,998
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

463
00:35:19,848 --> 00:35:21,975
(Robeson) It's got to be this one.

464
00:35:26,229 --> 00:35:29,524
(UNINTELLIGIBLE VOICES OF THE CHILDREN)

465
00:35:30,775 --> 00:35:31,943
There.

466
00:35:36,406 --> 00:35:39,450
(Robeson) Mara, grab her. Come on.

467
00:35:39,492 --> 00:35:40,702
Aria?

468
00:35:42,495 --> 00:35:44,682
- (Mara) Come with me, sweetheart.
- (Carl) Come on. Come on. Come on.

469
00:35:44,706 --> 00:35:46,666
(Robeson) Let's go. Let's go. Let's go.

470
00:35:49,919 --> 00:35:51,397
- (Robeson) Stay close.
- (Carl) Let's go.

471
00:35:51,421 --> 00:35:53,673
(Robeson) This way. This way!

472
00:35:54,257 --> 00:35:56,217
(Robeson) Hey, hey, get the fuck back!

473
00:35:57,760 --> 00:35:59,179
(THE MAN SPEAKS IN ALBANIAN)

474
00:36:00,680 --> 00:36:02,932
(A WOMAN SPEAKS IN ALBANIAN)

475
00:36:04,142 --> 00:36:06,978
(FIGHTING SOUNDS)

476
00:36:07,020 --> 00:36:09,439
(Robeson) Get off her! Hey! Get out!

477
00:36:09,480 --> 00:36:13,651
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

478
00:36:13,693 --> 00:36:16,946
- (Robeson) Hey! Get the fuck out!
- (Carl) Go, go, go!

479
00:36:16,988 --> 00:36:18,656
(SOMEONE SPEAKS IN ALBANIAN)

480
00:36:18,698 --> 00:36:20,325
(Carl) Against the wall.

481
00:36:20,366 --> 00:36:28,041
(FIGHTING SOUNDS)

482
00:36:28,082 --> 00:36:29,876
(Robeson) Come on, Let's go.

483
00:36:29,918 --> 00:36:32,170
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

484
00:36:32,212 --> 00:36:34,088
- (Carl) Let's go.
- (Robeson) Come on.

485
00:36:34,130 --> 00:36:38,343
(SOUNDS OF PAIN)

486
00:36:38,384 --> 00:36:41,346
- (Robeson) Come on, come on.
- (Carl) Come on.

487
00:36:41,387 --> 00:36:43,348
- (Mara) Come on, come on.
- (Robeson) Come on.

488
00:36:44,349 --> 00:36:46,351
(Robeson) Hey, we got to get to the car.

489
00:36:47,518 --> 00:36:49,398
(Robeson) Go, go, go.
(A MAN SPEAKS IN ALBANIAN)

490
00:36:49,437 --> 00:36:51,439
(Robeson) Hey, back. Back.

491
00:36:51,481 --> 00:36:54,484
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

492
00:36:54,525 --> 00:36:56,444
Stay back!

493
00:36:56,486 --> 00:37:01,574
(FIGHTING SOUNDS)

494
00:37:01,616 --> 00:37:03,701
- (WOMAN) Go, go!
- (Robeson) Stay back!

495
00:37:03,743 --> 00:37:11,743
(FIGHTING SOUNDS)

496
00:37:17,548 --> 00:37:19,717
(GUNSHOT)

497
00:37:19,759 --> 00:37:26,432
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

498
00:37:26,474 --> 00:37:28,893
- (Mara) Don't fucking touch me.
- (Robeson) Hey!

499
00:37:29,269 --> 00:37:31,271
Hey! Mara!

500
00:37:31,312 --> 00:37:34,482
(GUNSHOTS)

501
00:37:34,524 --> 00:37:37,527
Come on, run! We got to go. Go!

502
00:37:37,568 --> 00:37:40,280
- (Carl) Go, go, go, go!
- Go, go!

503
00:37:40,321 --> 00:37:44,033
(POLICE SIRENS)

504
00:37:48,705 --> 00:37:50,164
(Robeson) Fuck!

505
00:37:50,206 --> 00:37:51,666
Where's the transport?

506
00:37:52,333 --> 00:37:55,169
- (Carl) Mitch?
- He pulled the plane.

507
00:37:55,211 --> 00:37:56,838
(Carl) Who?

508
00:37:56,879 --> 00:37:58,548
Lewis.

509
00:38:00,133 --> 00:38:03,261
This is CIA?
Why the fuck didn't you tell us?

510
00:38:03,303 --> 00:38:05,221
CIA? What? Who's Lewis?

511
00:38:05,263 --> 00:38:08,266
- (Robeson) Hey. It was on a need to know basis.
- (Carl) Need to...

512
00:38:08,641 --> 00:38:12,186
- Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey, hey.
- I'm your partner! I'm in need to know!

513
00:38:12,228 --> 00:38:14,772
Stop it. What does this mean?

514
00:38:14,814 --> 00:38:19,527
It means the CIA got us to do a dirty job and now
that it's gone wrong, they're leaving us in it.

515
00:38:19,569 --> 00:38:22,071
Is that true? They're not going to help us?

516
00:38:22,113 --> 00:38:23,990
I'll figure it out.

517
00:38:24,532 --> 00:38:27,410
- I thought we worked for parents.
- We do.

518
00:38:27,452 --> 00:38:30,872
It's still a father getting back his
daughter, who pays us doesn't matter.

519
00:38:30,913 --> 00:38:32,874
Doesn't matter?

520
00:38:32,915 --> 00:38:36,919
What... what we do, who we
do it for is all the fucking matters.

521
00:38:38,504 --> 00:38:40,965
Get us the fuck out of here.

522
00:38:41,007 --> 00:38:49,007
(MELANCHOLIC MUSIC)

523
00:38:56,814 --> 00:38:58,667
<i>(JOE, on the phone) I hope you know</i>
what you're doing.

524
00:38:58,691 --> 00:39:00,818
(Mara) I'm helping people
get their kids back.

525
00:39:00,860 --> 00:39:03,696
<i>(JOE) And is this the best way</i>
to get Amina back?

526
00:39:04,655 --> 00:39:09,202
(Joe) Because you're just putting so much
trust in this thing. I just worry that...

527
00:39:09,744 --> 00:39:12,080
...you've lost track
of where you're trying to get to.

528
00:39:12,121 --> 00:39:15,375
Listen, I'll decide who or what I trust.

529
00:39:15,416 --> 00:39:17,877
<i>(Mara) I have to go. Love you.</i>

530
00:39:20,797 --> 00:39:25,676
(Mara) Then 500 feet
and the venue is on the left.

531
00:39:25,718 --> 00:39:29,389
At least I think, it's a little unclear.

532
00:39:29,430 --> 00:39:32,141
- Yeah, Carl's out taking photos.
- Okay.

533
00:39:32,433 --> 00:39:35,061
(Mara) Main entrance is on the main road.

534
00:39:35,103 --> 00:39:39,774
But there's another way on the corner
that takes us to the kitchen.

535
00:39:43,027 --> 00:39:46,364
- What?
- You're kind of a natural at this.

536
00:39:53,121 --> 00:39:56,165
What if we're giving
her to the wrong parent?

537
00:39:56,207 --> 00:39:58,418
What if the mother is no good?

538
00:39:58,459 --> 00:40:00,294
Where's this going?

539
00:40:06,217 --> 00:40:08,344
I almost got rid of her.

540
00:40:08,386 --> 00:40:09,720
Amina.

541
00:40:09,762 --> 00:40:12,140
(Mara) And now I can't
bear to live without her.

542
00:40:12,807 --> 00:40:18,104
I met Karim in the hospital, I had all
these problems with my hands and feet.

543
00:40:18,146 --> 00:40:20,356
He did all my scans.

544
00:40:20,398 --> 00:40:22,692
(Mara) We started
seeing each other after that.

545
00:40:22,733 --> 00:40:25,945
(Mara) He was kind and
funny and took care of me.

546
00:40:25,987 --> 00:40:29,824
Made me feel safe.
I never intended to get pregnant.

547
00:40:29,866 --> 00:40:32,160
I freaked out.

548
00:40:32,201 --> 00:40:35,746
(Mara) I left Karim a message,
and I drove myself to the clinic.

549
00:40:35,788 --> 00:40:40,751
Right when I was about to sign the papers,
Karim came rushing in...

550
00:40:40,793 --> 00:40:43,796
...just... full of passion.

551
00:40:43,838 --> 00:40:46,424
That's what he was like
about the things that he loves.

552
00:40:46,466 --> 00:40:50,970
He said: "We can do
this. It's going to be okay".

553
00:40:52,221 --> 00:40:54,390
And it was. For a while.

554
00:40:55,683 --> 00:40:59,896
Then he started acting really weird,
staying out late.

555
00:41:00,897 --> 00:41:07,153
Wanted me to quit my job.
I started drinking too much, I guess.

556
00:41:07,195 --> 00:41:11,073
I mean, it's not really your fault.
You didn't really know the guy.

557
00:41:11,741 --> 00:41:14,869
How do you know
what I should be punishing myself for?

558
00:41:15,828 --> 00:41:17,330
Okay.

559
00:41:17,371 --> 00:41:19,290
Here's what I do know.

560
00:41:19,832 --> 00:41:23,419
Parents, they need you on these jobs.

561
00:41:23,461 --> 00:41:27,673
(ROMANTIC MUSIC)

562
00:41:27,715 --> 00:41:29,675
What about you?

563
00:41:29,717 --> 00:41:31,135
(ROMANTIC MUSIC)

564
00:41:31,177 --> 00:41:33,012
Do you need me?

565
00:41:33,054 --> 00:41:37,558
(ROMANTIC MUSIC)

566
00:41:37,600 --> 00:41:42,355
(SOUNDS OF KISSING)

567
00:41:42,396 --> 00:41:45,900
(ROMANTIC MUSIC)

568
00:41:45,942 --> 00:41:53,942
(SOUNDS OF KISSING)

569
00:41:55,660 --> 00:42:03,660
(SAD MUSIC)

570
00:42:17,890 --> 00:42:22,603
(TELEPHONE RINGING)

571
00:42:23,813 --> 00:42:25,523
Robeson.

572
00:42:27,525 --> 00:42:35,525
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

573
00:42:44,166 --> 00:42:45,960
What have you got?

574
00:42:46,002 --> 00:42:54,002
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

575
00:42:56,012 --> 00:42:59,098
- What about Romania?
- I'm working on it.

576
00:42:59,140 --> 00:43:01,559
Petra's father really
wants his daughter back.

577
00:43:01,601 --> 00:43:04,437
She's the most important thing
in the world to him.

578
00:43:04,478 --> 00:43:10,359
(Lewis) I don't object to your private cases, but
not at the expense of what the CIA needs from you.

579
00:43:10,401 --> 00:43:12,862
Okay, well, I think
I'm helping these parents, too.

580
00:43:12,903 --> 00:43:15,323
And I'm sure that they are very grateful.

581
00:43:15,364 --> 00:43:18,951
But you're a military man,
so I know that you understand...

582
00:43:18,993 --> 00:43:23,205
...the plight of housewives and
grandparents is not quite as vital...

583
00:43:23,247 --> 00:43:26,083
...as keeping this country
and its assets safe.

584
00:43:26,125 --> 00:43:30,880
Stop deprioritizing my cases,
Mitchell, or you won't have any.

585
00:43:31,756 --> 00:43:36,177
(Robeson) All right, I'll move
Romania to the top of the list.

586
00:43:37,053 --> 00:43:39,930
- (Lewis) How're things going with Danning?
- (Robeson) Good.

587
00:43:39,972 --> 00:43:42,558
- (Lewis) She's still looking for her kid.
- (Robeson) Of course.

588
00:43:43,017 --> 00:43:46,437
(Lewis) Just remember to keep
the trail cold for as long as possible.

589
00:43:46,854 --> 00:43:48,773
Why would you say that?

590
00:43:48,814 --> 00:43:52,068
Karim Taleb is a dangerous man.

591
00:43:52,109 --> 00:43:54,487
(Lewis) She's better
off without him in her life.

592
00:43:54,528 --> 00:43:56,447
How dangerous, Lewis?

593
00:43:56,489 --> 00:44:00,409
That's classified.
You do your job and I'll do mine.

594
00:44:00,451 --> 00:44:04,914
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

595
00:44:04,955 --> 00:44:08,417
- Hi. Do you speak English?
<i>- (Female operator) Yes, ma'am.</i>

596
00:44:08,459 --> 00:44:10,586
Thank you. Ehm...

597
00:44:10,628 --> 00:44:13,923
(Mara) I have a patient at your hospital,
but I can't read his chart.

598
00:44:13,964 --> 00:44:17,051
I can only read the
name of the radiologist.

599
00:44:17,093 --> 00:44:21,681
Can I speak to him, please?
His name's Karim Taleb.

600
00:44:21,722 --> 00:44:24,266
<i>- (Female operator) One minute, please.</i>
- Mm-mm.

601
00:44:25,893 --> 00:44:29,939
<i>(Female operator) He is not working today.</i>
Would you like to leave him a message?

602
00:44:29,980 --> 00:44:32,149
- Taleb?
<i>- (Female operator) Yes.</i>

603
00:44:32,191 --> 00:44:35,486
(Mara) T-A-L-E-B.

604
00:44:35,528 --> 00:44:37,279
(Mara) He does?

605
00:44:37,905 --> 00:44:39,699
That's him?

606
00:44:40,074 --> 00:44:41,534
That's him!

607
00:44:41,575 --> 00:44:44,745
- What? Amina?
- (crying) My God.

608
00:44:44,787 --> 00:44:47,289
(CHEERFUL MUSIC)

609
00:44:48,457 --> 00:44:56,457
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

610
00:45:08,102 --> 00:45:09,979
(SOUND OF THE DOORBELL)

611
00:45:10,771 --> 00:45:13,023
(SOUND OF A DOOR OPENING)

612
00:45:24,201 --> 00:45:25,745
(Mara) Come on.

613
00:45:33,043 --> 00:45:41,043
(SOUNDS OF POLICE SIRENS)

614
00:45:46,140 --> 00:45:47,725
(SMACKING KISS)

615
00:45:47,767 --> 00:45:50,102
- (Robeson) Mm...
- Mitchell.

616
00:45:52,354 --> 00:45:54,482
- Mitchell.
- (Robeson) Mm-mm?

617
00:45:54,523 --> 00:45:57,651
I found him. Karim is in Lebanon.

618
00:46:00,654 --> 00:46:02,031
(Robeson) How did you?

619
00:46:02,072 --> 00:46:05,034
I tracked him down
to a hospital just outside Beirut.

620
00:46:05,075 --> 00:46:07,661
He's been working there for a whole year.

621
00:46:07,703 --> 00:46:10,956
- Are you sure?
- Oh, Jesus Christ, Mitch.

622
00:46:10,998 --> 00:46:15,878
Do you know how many calls I've made to
hospitals in Syria and surrounding countries?

623
00:46:15,920 --> 00:46:21,133
Hundreds. And suddenly,
just like that, there he fucking is.

624
00:46:21,175 --> 00:46:23,344
He didn't even change his name.

625
00:46:25,179 --> 00:46:29,475
Oh, so that's what this is.
You come over. Use me.

626
00:46:30,142 --> 00:46:33,896
(Mara) No. This is the
best lead I've ever had.

627
00:46:33,938 --> 00:46:36,774
- I just want to get out there.
- What am I always telling you?

628
00:46:36,816 --> 00:46:40,069
- You have to stop and think!
- Don't fucking yell at me.

629
00:46:40,110 --> 00:46:42,947
This is finally something real for me.

630
00:46:42,988 --> 00:46:45,157
Okay. I'm sorry. I didn't...

631
00:46:45,699 --> 00:46:46,951
You're right.

632
00:46:47,743 --> 00:46:52,289
It's a good lead.
But you won't go out there on your own.

633
00:46:53,374 --> 00:46:58,295
(Robeson) So when the time is right, we'll do
it like all the others. Planned. Rehearsed.

634
00:46:58,337 --> 00:47:02,633
And when will be the right time, Mitch?
Because you keep saying that.

635
00:47:03,592 --> 00:47:07,304
The fucking time is now.
We need to get out there.

636
00:47:07,346 --> 00:47:09,807
Is the Beirut job still on the table?

637
00:47:09,849 --> 00:47:12,059
No. The Beirut job is too risky.

638
00:47:12,101 --> 00:47:16,564
So you take it, and then the client will pay
for you to pull strings to get us out there.

639
00:47:19,358 --> 00:47:21,193
Please.

640
00:47:21,235 --> 00:47:24,989
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

641
00:47:25,030 --> 00:47:28,617
So, as far as we can
tell, exit points are here.

642
00:47:28,659 --> 00:47:32,872
And the rear trade entrance. That'll be
our best bet to avoid our private security.

643
00:47:32,913 --> 00:47:36,917
Right. Well, we only have one
invite, so it will have to be me.

644
00:47:36,959 --> 00:47:39,378
You get trapped,
you have to fight your way out alone.

645
00:47:39,420 --> 00:47:42,673
- Yeah. I've done it before.
- No.

646
00:47:42,715 --> 00:47:44,466
- I don't like it.
- What?

647
00:47:44,508 --> 00:47:49,054
You're kidding, right? It's the perfect setup
and the biggest score we've ever gotten.

648
00:47:49,096 --> 00:47:51,473
You know Lebanon is still unstable, right?

649
00:47:51,515 --> 00:47:55,561
Beirut is militarized, and these people
have money for private guards.

650
00:47:55,603 --> 00:48:00,482
I'm the one that has to get us out if all
goes to shit. Nah, this is a no go for me.

651
00:48:00,524 --> 00:48:02,818
No. I may never have
another chance to get out there.

652
00:48:02,860 --> 00:48:07,114
- We'll find another way.
- It's been eight years. Eight fucking years!

653
00:48:07,156 --> 00:48:09,909
How much more time
do you think I can wait?

654
00:48:11,076 --> 00:48:13,162
(Robeson) Jesus Christ.

655
00:48:13,203 --> 00:48:20,836
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

656
00:48:20,878 --> 00:48:22,963
- What the fuck was that?
- I told you.

657
00:48:23,005 --> 00:48:24,590
I don't like it. It feels dangerous.

658
00:48:24,632 --> 00:48:27,051
More dangerous than taking kids
from rich-as-fuck statesmen?

659
00:48:27,092 --> 00:48:29,720
Maybe she's better off
if she lets this whole Lebanon lead go.

660
00:48:29,762 --> 00:48:31,472
Are you serious?

661
00:48:31,513 --> 00:48:34,558
She's done all those jobs with us
because you made her a promise...

662
00:48:34,600 --> 00:48:37,019
...that one of them would be her own kid.

663
00:48:38,604 --> 00:48:42,983
Imagine that, Mitch,
having a mother who loved you that much.

664
00:48:43,651 --> 00:48:46,320
I sure as shit wouldn't have ended up here.

665
00:48:49,406 --> 00:48:53,535
Come on, man.
Help us figure out the snatch.

666
00:48:53,577 --> 00:48:56,330
Then we'll go out there,
do it as well as we usually do it...

667
00:48:56,372 --> 00:48:59,291
...and then afterwards
we'll help her get her daughter back.

668
00:49:00,584 --> 00:49:02,127
(Carl) Okay?

669
00:49:02,169 --> 00:49:05,506
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

670
00:49:05,547 --> 00:49:08,008
Come on, man, fuckin' do this.

671
00:49:08,050 --> 00:49:09,927
(Robeson) Okay.

672
00:49:11,345 --> 00:49:13,514
- (Robeson) We're good.
- What?

673
00:49:14,598 --> 00:49:18,644
You better know this house inside and out.
Every room, every exit.

674
00:49:19,770 --> 00:49:22,564
And this one's by the book.
My rules. Okay?

675
00:49:22,606 --> 00:49:24,066
(Mara) Yeah.

676
00:49:24,608 --> 00:49:25,859
(Robeson) Yeah.

677
00:49:25,901 --> 00:49:27,486
(Mara) Thank you.

678
00:49:28,028 --> 00:49:29,488
(Robeson) Okay.

679
00:49:29,530 --> 00:49:32,658
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

680
00:49:32,700 --> 00:49:34,284
It's for you.

681
00:49:34,326 --> 00:49:41,500
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

682
00:49:41,542 --> 00:49:45,212
(HEAVY BREATHING)

683
00:49:45,254 --> 00:49:48,007
(Joe) I've waited
as long as I could for Amina.

684
00:49:49,842 --> 00:49:54,054
When your mom left, remember?

685
00:49:54,096 --> 00:49:56,432
I didn't know...

686
00:49:56,473 --> 00:49:59,643
...whether either of us would be okay.

687
00:49:59,685 --> 00:50:03,731
(Joe) You were so tiny. Remember?

688
00:50:03,772 --> 00:50:06,859
(Joe) I took you to the park.

689
00:50:06,900 --> 00:50:11,905
You climbed a jungle gym and you fell off.

690
00:50:11,947 --> 00:50:14,283
I bashed my teeth.

691
00:50:14,324 --> 00:50:18,620
(Joe, whining) And that woman,
she came...

692
00:50:18,662 --> 00:50:20,497
...rushing over.

693
00:50:20,539 --> 00:50:26,628
(Joe) She said: "Where is your mother?"
And you said...

694
00:50:27,212 --> 00:50:32,468
"My mom's gone.
But my dad's here and we're just fine."

695
00:50:32,509 --> 00:50:34,219
(JOE SIGHS)

696
00:50:34,261 --> 00:50:40,225
That's when I knew
you would always be okay.

697
00:50:41,685 --> 00:50:45,147
- You have to be strong for me.
- (crying) No.

698
00:50:45,189 --> 00:50:48,108
(crying) Dad, please, no.

699
00:50:48,150 --> 00:50:54,448
You tell her I love her so much.

700
00:50:54,490 --> 00:50:59,119
(JOE BREATHS HEAVILY)
(crying) Hey, dad, dad...

701
00:51:00,412 --> 00:51:02,498
I need to rest now.

702
00:51:02,539 --> 00:51:04,833
(SAD MUSIC)

703
00:51:04,875 --> 00:51:06,543
(Mara) Yeah.

704
00:51:06,585 --> 00:51:11,882
(MARA CRIES AND JOE BREATHS HEAVILY)

705
00:51:16,386 --> 00:51:24,386
(SAD MUSIC)

706
00:51:46,041 --> 00:51:52,714
(SOUNDS OF THE PLANE LEAVING)

707
00:51:52,756 --> 00:52:00,756
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

708
00:52:25,998 --> 00:52:31,503
(FAINT VOICES)

709
00:52:31,545 --> 00:52:37,426
(ORIENTAL MUSIC)

710
00:52:37,467 --> 00:52:39,803
(UNINTELLIGIBLE VOICES IN ARABIC)

711
00:52:39,845 --> 00:52:47,352
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

712
00:52:48,437 --> 00:52:49,980
(SOUND OF A DOOR OPENING)

713
00:52:50,022 --> 00:52:51,773
You okay?

714
00:52:52,649 --> 00:52:55,277
Hi! Mama!

715
00:52:55,319 --> 00:52:57,654
- Who are you and what did you do with Soraya?
- Hey!

716
00:52:57,696 --> 00:53:00,824
You're so tall.
Get over here. Your mom's here?

717
00:53:00,866 --> 00:53:02,451
Yeah.

718
00:53:02,951 --> 00:53:05,078
(Dasia) Oh!

719
00:53:05,120 --> 00:53:08,373
(A MAN AND DASIA SPEAK IN ARABIC)

720
00:53:08,415 --> 00:53:10,250
(Robeson) It's so good to see you.

721
00:53:11,460 --> 00:53:14,296
- Oh, long time.
- Too long, Dasia.

722
00:53:14,963 --> 00:53:17,674
- This is Mara.
- (Dasia) Hi. - Hi.

723
00:53:17,716 --> 00:53:21,470
Soraya, go and get the tea. Please.

724
00:53:23,972 --> 00:53:25,557
(Robeson) Nothing changed around here.

725
00:53:25,599 --> 00:53:29,853
(Dasia) No, it's like a zoo in here
sometimes. I hope you don't mind.

726
00:53:29,895 --> 00:53:32,397
- But you'll be sleeping in the living room.
- Oh, no.

727
00:53:32,439 --> 00:53:35,359
I didn't want you
to have to share with the men.

728
00:53:35,400 --> 00:53:37,736
That's very thoughtful. Thank you.

729
00:53:37,778 --> 00:53:39,446
Come on.

730
00:53:44,952 --> 00:53:50,958
(Dasia) Robeson told me that your ex-husband
is living here. You are okay to talk about it?

731
00:53:50,999 --> 00:53:52,876
Yeah, of course.

732
00:53:54,211 --> 00:53:57,339
- For you.
- Oh, thank you. Thank you.

733
00:53:58,465 --> 00:53:59,800
Please.

734
00:54:01,718 --> 00:54:04,471
- (Mara) She's wonderful.
- (Dasia) They grow so fast.

735
00:54:04,930 --> 00:54:07,140
Do you know where your ex works?

736
00:54:07,182 --> 00:54:12,688
At a hospital just outside the city, I
think. But I don't know where he lives.

737
00:54:13,772 --> 00:54:15,857
I'll take you there tomorrow.

738
00:54:16,608 --> 00:54:18,944
See if we can find out.

739
00:54:21,613 --> 00:54:27,911
(TRAFFIC SOUNDS)

740
00:54:27,953 --> 00:54:35,953
(CHEERFUL MUSIC)

741
00:54:36,586 --> 00:54:38,005
Hey.

742
00:54:38,046 --> 00:54:39,923
(CHEERFUL MUSIC)

743
00:54:39,965 --> 00:54:44,845
(Mara) I think I might finally be under
the same little patch of stars that she is.

744
00:54:44,886 --> 00:54:50,767
(CHEERFUL MUSIC)

745
00:54:50,809 --> 00:54:53,020
I know you feel close to her.

746
00:54:53,061 --> 00:54:55,147
(CHEERFUL MUSIC)

747
00:54:55,188 --> 00:54:59,109
I really need you focused
on this job first. Okay?

748
00:54:59,901 --> 00:55:01,570
I know.

749
00:55:01,611 --> 00:55:09,611
(CHEERFUL MUSIC)

750
00:55:13,332 --> 00:55:19,087
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

751
00:55:19,129 --> 00:55:21,840
(UNINTELLIGIBLE VOICES)

752
00:55:21,882 --> 00:55:29,882
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

753
00:55:42,778 --> 00:55:46,740
He was on a temporary contract.
He's not here anymore.

754
00:55:46,782 --> 00:55:52,371
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

755
00:55:52,412 --> 00:55:55,624
Hey. It's a process.

756
00:55:55,665 --> 00:55:58,126
He's in the city.

757
00:55:58,168 --> 00:56:00,337
We're going to find him.

758
00:56:07,427 --> 00:56:12,474
(ROCK MUSIC)

759
00:56:26,780 --> 00:56:29,699
- Can you move in it?
- Think so.

760
00:56:29,741 --> 00:56:31,576
Yeah.

761
00:56:34,413 --> 00:56:36,623
(Robeson) Okay. No heroics tonight.

762
00:56:40,335 --> 00:56:43,046
(Robeson) Grab the kid
and you get out of there.

763
00:56:43,380 --> 00:56:45,882
(Robeson) Be careful, Mara.

764
00:56:45,924 --> 00:56:53,924
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

765
00:56:59,563 --> 00:57:04,818
(FAINT VOICES)

766
00:57:04,860 --> 00:57:07,028
(THE BODYGUARD SPEAKS IN ARABIC)

767
00:57:07,070 --> 00:57:11,241
(FAINT VOICES)

768
00:57:11,283 --> 00:57:12,993
Thank you.

769
00:57:13,034 --> 00:57:15,454
(FAINT VOICES AND MUSIC)

770
00:57:15,495 --> 00:57:17,414
(Isra) As-salam alaykom.

771
00:57:18,790 --> 00:57:21,001
Wa Alykom As-slam.

772
00:57:21,042 --> 00:57:25,589
- Are you from the embassy?
- Oh, God, no. Fuck politics. I'm in finance.

773
00:57:26,506 --> 00:57:29,050
(Isra) Oh, excellent.

774
00:57:29,092 --> 00:57:33,472
Please do tell me if you need
an introduction to any of my other guests.

775
00:57:33,513 --> 00:57:35,557
That is so kind of you.

776
00:57:35,599 --> 00:57:38,935
In the meantime, could you point me
the direction of the ladies room?

777
00:57:38,977 --> 00:57:42,105
- It's down the hall.
- Thank you. Oh!

778
00:57:42,147 --> 00:57:44,649
Shukran jaziilan.

779
00:57:44,691 --> 00:57:47,486
(FAINT VOICES)

780
00:57:47,527 --> 00:57:55,527
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

781
00:58:06,171 --> 00:58:14,171
(VOICES FROM A TV)

782
00:58:16,556 --> 00:58:24,556
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

783
00:58:28,735 --> 00:58:32,697
(VOICES FROM THE TV)

784
00:58:32,739 --> 00:58:36,952
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

785
00:58:45,752 --> 00:58:48,630
(SOME PEOPLE SPEAK IN ARABIC)

786
00:58:48,672 --> 00:58:50,966
(Mara) Come on. There's a good girl.

787
00:58:51,800 --> 00:58:54,427
Okay, let's go. Come on.

788
00:58:54,469 --> 00:59:02,469
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

789
00:59:10,151 --> 00:59:11,945
It's gonna be okay.

790
00:59:11,987 --> 00:59:19,987
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

791
00:59:21,496 --> 00:59:27,377
(VOICES IN ARABIC FROM THE KITCHEN)

792
00:59:27,419 --> 00:59:35,419
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

793
00:59:45,520 --> 00:59:48,857
What are you doing with my daughter?

794
00:59:49,441 --> 00:59:52,694
- I'm not going to hurt her.
- You're taking her away from me?

795
00:59:52,736 --> 00:59:55,447
(SALMA WHINES)

796
01:00:00,619 --> 01:00:06,625
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

797
01:00:06,666 --> 01:00:08,627
(Mara) Don't.

798
01:00:08,668 --> 01:00:10,837
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

799
01:00:10,879 --> 01:00:12,631
Salma, come.

800
01:00:12,672 --> 01:00:15,258
(GUNSHOTS)

801
01:00:15,300 --> 01:00:17,802
(SALMA SCREAMS)

802
01:00:17,844 --> 01:00:21,848
(SOUNDS OF PAIN)

803
01:00:21,890 --> 01:00:23,642
Salma.

804
01:00:25,477 --> 01:00:27,687
- (Isra) Oh...
- Oh my God.

805
01:00:27,729 --> 01:00:31,566
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

806
01:00:31,608 --> 01:00:33,443
Is that her?

807
01:00:33,485 --> 01:00:41,284
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

808
01:00:41,326 --> 01:00:43,411
- You okay?
- Drive!

809
01:00:43,453 --> 01:00:46,247
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

810
01:00:46,289 --> 01:00:47,749
(THE GUARDS SPEAK IN ARABIC)

811
01:00:47,791 --> 01:00:49,793
(Carl) I see 'em, hang on.

812
01:00:50,835 --> 01:00:52,545
(Mara) I got you, baby.

813
01:00:53,004 --> 01:00:54,881
(THE MEN SPEAK IN ARABIC)

814
01:00:54,923 --> 01:00:57,175
(Robeson) Get down!
(GUNSHOTS)

815
01:00:57,217 --> 01:00:59,052
(Robeson) Keep your heads down!

816
01:00:59,094 --> 01:01:02,389
(GUNSHOTS)

817
01:01:02,430 --> 01:01:04,808
(Robeson) One way. Watch out! Shit.

818
01:01:04,849 --> 01:01:08,728
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

819
01:01:08,770 --> 01:01:10,814
What happened in there?

820
01:01:10,855 --> 01:01:13,274
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

821
01:01:13,316 --> 01:01:15,318
(Robeson) Mara, are you going to tell us?

822
01:01:15,360 --> 01:01:21,199
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

823
01:01:25,328 --> 01:01:31,292
(DRAMATIC MUSIC)

824
01:01:31,334 --> 01:01:33,461
(Mara) That's a good girl.

825
01:01:33,503 --> 01:01:36,172
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

826
01:01:36,214 --> 01:01:37,757
Alright...

827
01:01:37,799 --> 01:01:45,799
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

828
01:01:47,976 --> 01:01:50,145
That's a good girl.

829
01:01:50,186 --> 01:01:53,606
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

830
01:01:53,648 --> 01:01:55,525
Okay, it's okay.

831
01:01:55,567 --> 01:01:57,986
(SOUND OF A CAR APPROACHING)

832
01:02:03,616 --> 01:02:05,326
(Robeson) He's here.

833
01:02:05,368 --> 01:02:10,790
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

834
01:02:10,832 --> 01:02:13,334
(SALMA SPEAKS IN ARABIC)
(Robeson) Of course.

835
01:02:14,085 --> 01:02:15,396
(THE MAN SAYS SOMETHING IN ARABIC)

836
01:02:15,420 --> 01:02:17,380
(MAN) Thank you so much.

837
01:02:17,422 --> 01:02:23,178
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

838
01:02:23,219 --> 01:02:29,809
(WATER RUNNING IN THE SHOWER)

839
01:02:29,851 --> 01:02:31,811
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

840
01:02:31,853 --> 01:02:34,230
(SOUND OF THE DOOR OPENING)

841
01:02:34,272 --> 01:02:38,234
(WATER RUNNING IN THE SHOWER)

842
01:02:38,276 --> 01:02:40,612
It was an accident, Mara.

843
01:02:45,116 --> 01:02:47,869
You're not going to let me look
for Amina anymore, are you?

844
01:02:47,911 --> 01:02:55,911
(WATER RUNNING IN THE SHOWER)

845
01:03:01,341 --> 01:03:04,385
(Robeson) Okay, I'm going out.
See if I can find us a way home.

846
01:03:04,427 --> 01:03:06,137
- I'll come.
- (Robeson) No.

847
01:03:06,179 --> 01:03:11,142
It's not safe. Stay here at the hotel. At least
until I can find out if we're in the clear.

848
01:03:12,268 --> 01:03:14,771
(SOUND OF THE DOOR OPENING AND CLOSING)

849
01:03:14,813 --> 01:03:22,813
(FAINT VOICES)

850
01:03:24,781 --> 01:03:31,621
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

851
01:03:31,663 --> 01:03:33,414
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

852
01:03:41,506 --> 01:03:43,383
(Carl) Who is it?

853
01:03:43,424 --> 01:03:45,802
- (Dasia) Dasia.
- It's Dasia.

854
01:03:47,262 --> 01:03:49,889
- (Dasia) Dasia!
- Okay, okay, okay. Hey.

855
01:03:50,598 --> 01:03:52,976
- Hey.
- (Carl) Hey.

856
01:03:55,103 --> 01:03:57,564
- You shouldn't be here.
- I have a lead.

857
01:03:57,605 --> 01:03:59,107
On what?

858
01:03:59,899 --> 01:04:01,734
On Amina.

859
01:04:02,318 --> 01:04:04,421
- (Carl) No. No. Wait for Robeson.
- (Mara) We have to go.

860
01:04:04,445 --> 01:04:07,824
No. You know, a lead
only lasts so long. I'll go by myself.

861
01:04:07,866 --> 01:04:11,411
- No. You heard what he said.
- A couple of hours, tops.

862
01:04:11,452 --> 01:04:13,746
Then at least we'll have some intel.

863
01:04:13,788 --> 01:04:16,416
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

864
01:04:16,457 --> 01:04:18,209
Shit.

865
01:04:18,251 --> 01:04:19,669
(FAINT VOICES)

866
01:04:19,711 --> 01:04:21,087
(Dasia) You should wait here.

867
01:04:22,422 --> 01:04:24,924
- In and out. Okay?
- (Dasia) Yeah. Okay.

868
01:04:24,966 --> 01:04:30,763
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

869
01:04:30,805 --> 01:04:32,599
(Robeson) What are you doing out here?

870
01:04:32,640 --> 01:04:34,601
This is my territory.

871
01:04:36,102 --> 01:04:38,479
(Lewis) The more pertinent question is:...

872
01:04:38,521 --> 01:04:43,776
...what the hell are you doing out here
and not in Romania, like I ordered you to?

873
01:04:46,529 --> 01:04:49,782
And at the center of all this is Denning...

874
01:04:49,824 --> 01:04:53,578
...who's compromised us with a snatch back
caught up in a bloodbath.

875
01:04:53,620 --> 01:04:55,830
(Lewis) A woman who shouldn't be
anywhere near here...

876
01:04:55,872 --> 01:04:59,226
...but is at risk of destroying everything
that I've worked for the last eight years.

877
01:04:59,250 --> 01:05:01,687
And a woman who's the only one
who could've gotten us in and out.

878
01:05:01,711 --> 01:05:03,671
- Is that right?
- (Robeson) That's right.

879
01:05:03,713 --> 01:05:07,258
And you're telling me
that you had to take a job in Beirut?

880
01:05:08,509 --> 01:05:11,054
She goes to school
with her youngest granddaughter.

881
01:05:12,138 --> 01:05:14,849
(Mara) Where? Have you met her? Amina.

882
01:05:14,891 --> 01:05:17,560
(Dasia, in Arabic) Have you met Amina?

883
01:05:17,602 --> 01:05:21,230
(Grandmother, in Arabic) Once.
She is... Rather a rebel, I think.

884
01:05:21,272 --> 01:05:25,860
Once. She thinks that
Amina is rather a rebel.

885
01:05:25,902 --> 01:05:29,489
Is she? That's good.

886
01:05:29,530 --> 01:05:33,201
(DASIA SAYS SOMETHING IN ARABIC)

887
01:05:33,242 --> 01:05:35,620
(Mara) What time do the schools finish?

888
01:05:35,662 --> 01:05:38,790
- At 3:00 p.m...
- Okay, could she give me an address?

889
01:05:38,831 --> 01:05:43,711
Robeson, let me make it absolutely clear to
you, as you don't seem to have got the message.

890
01:05:43,753 --> 01:05:48,967
It is imperative to my interests
and therefore to yours...

891
01:05:49,008 --> 01:05:51,719
...that she does not find Karim Taleb.

892
01:05:51,761 --> 01:05:55,807
So when you asked me
to stop looking into Karim, I did.

893
01:05:55,848 --> 01:05:58,685
But if you expect me to keep that mother
from her daughter...

894
01:05:58,726 --> 01:06:01,938
...you better tell me
what the fuck's really going on right now.

895
01:06:01,980 --> 01:06:04,816
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

896
01:06:04,857 --> 01:06:07,819
How much do you know
about your husband's life here?

897
01:06:07,860 --> 01:06:10,738
What do you know
about your husband's life here?

898
01:06:10,780 --> 01:06:12,991
I mean, nothing. Why?

899
01:06:13,032 --> 01:06:14,951
(Dasia, in Arabic) Why do you ask?

900
01:06:14,993 --> 01:06:18,746
- (in Arabic) - It's late. I should go.
- Why? Wait.

901
01:06:19,622 --> 01:06:21,290
She should leave.

902
01:06:21,332 --> 01:06:24,585
(in Arabic) Wait. Give
her the address. Please?

903
01:06:24,627 --> 01:06:28,172
- (in Arabic) I can't.
- (Mara) Please, please. As a mother.

904
01:06:32,510 --> 01:06:36,472
(in Arabic) As a mother, I tell you
to go see your daughter.

905
01:06:36,514 --> 01:06:39,058
See that she is well, but
then you should leave.

906
01:06:39,100 --> 01:06:44,897
As a mother she tells you: Go see your daughter,
see that she is fine. But then you should leave.

907
01:06:46,566 --> 01:06:50,194
(Grandmother) The enemy
of my enemy is my friend.

908
01:06:51,529 --> 01:06:53,322
(Grandmother) Good luck.

909
01:06:53,364 --> 01:07:00,872
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

910
01:07:00,913 --> 01:07:05,501
Listen. I cannot come to the school. I cannot
bring trouble to my family. Do you understand?

911
01:07:05,543 --> 01:07:07,378
Of course. Of course.

912
01:07:07,420 --> 01:07:12,008
You've done more to help me in a few days
than anyone in my own country did for years.

913
01:07:12,050 --> 01:07:13,843
Go.

914
01:07:14,594 --> 01:07:17,055
- (Robeson) You had me lie to her.
- No.

915
01:07:17,889 --> 01:07:20,224
It's not lying if you
didn't have all the facts.

916
01:07:20,266 --> 01:07:22,185
- (Lewis) Oh!
- Fuck you.

917
01:07:22,226 --> 01:07:24,145
I tipped you off to her...

918
01:07:24,187 --> 01:07:27,607
...so you could give her an opportunity
to get involved in something, right?

919
01:07:27,648 --> 01:07:30,068
- Distract her.
- Something that would give her life purpose.

920
01:07:30,109 --> 01:07:32,695
- And then you let her lead you right here.
- You used me.

921
01:07:32,737 --> 01:07:36,115
You need to convince her
that the leads she has are false...

922
01:07:36,157 --> 01:07:38,052
...and you need to get her
out of the country immediately.

923
01:07:38,076 --> 01:07:39,535
And if I don't?

924
01:07:39,577 --> 01:07:43,206
Then I can't guarantee
that she or her family will be safe.

925
01:07:43,247 --> 01:07:44,665
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

926
01:07:44,707 --> 01:07:47,043
- From you.
- From anybody.

927
01:07:47,085 --> 01:07:51,839
Her desperation is making the situation
unstable. And that's when people get hurt.

928
01:07:52,340 --> 01:07:55,468
Do you really want that
on your conscience?

929
01:07:56,511 --> 01:08:02,183
I need you to serve your country right now,
not her. I know you understand that.

930
01:08:02,850 --> 01:08:05,645
And never put your hands
on me like that again.

931
01:08:05,686 --> 01:08:10,691
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

932
01:08:14,028 --> 01:08:16,197
It's it.

933
01:08:16,239 --> 01:08:21,869
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

934
01:08:25,957 --> 01:08:30,169
It looks pretty secure.
Heavy gates, guards, CCTV.

935
01:08:31,879 --> 01:08:34,340
No back entrance.

936
01:08:34,382 --> 01:08:36,050
School got out 10 minutes ago.

937
01:08:37,385 --> 01:08:39,762
So she lives?

938
01:08:42,557 --> 01:08:45,518
- Hey.
- What?

939
01:08:45,560 --> 01:08:51,232
(FAINT VOICES)

940
01:08:51,274 --> 01:08:53,067
(Carl) Is that her?

941
01:08:53,109 --> 01:09:01,109
(CHEERFUL MUSIC)

942
01:09:04,245 --> 01:09:08,082
(NON AUDIBLE DIALOGUES)

943
01:09:08,124 --> 01:09:16,124
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

944
01:09:21,762 --> 01:09:25,725
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

945
01:09:26,976 --> 01:09:30,855
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

946
01:09:30,897 --> 01:09:34,192
Hey, hey, hey! They'll see you.
Shut the door.

947
01:09:36,861 --> 01:09:41,616
We have no plan. Anything you do now,
we just tip them off and ruin everything.

948
01:09:42,825 --> 01:09:45,036
Hide your face.

949
01:09:45,077 --> 01:09:53,077
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

950
01:10:01,177 --> 01:10:09,177
(FAINT VOICES)

951
01:10:10,853 --> 01:10:18,853
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

952
01:10:19,403 --> 01:10:23,115
No! Hey! Hey! Fuck.

953
01:10:23,157 --> 01:10:27,245
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

954
01:10:27,286 --> 01:10:30,957
(FAINT VOICES AND TRADITIONAL MUSIC)

955
01:10:34,085 --> 01:10:38,965
(FAINT VOICES)

956
01:10:39,006 --> 01:10:41,842
(KARIM, AMINA
AND HER GRANDFATHER TALK IN ARABIC)

957
01:10:41,884 --> 01:10:47,515
(FAINT VOICES)

958
01:10:47,556 --> 01:10:50,142
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

959
01:10:50,184 --> 01:10:52,103
(NON AUDIBLE DIALOGUES)

960
01:10:52,144 --> 01:10:55,147
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

961
01:10:55,189 --> 01:10:59,610
(AMINA AND HER GRANDFATHER TALK IN ARABIC)

962
01:10:59,652 --> 01:11:06,492
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

963
01:11:06,534 --> 01:11:14,083
(NON AUDIBLE DIALOGUES)

964
01:11:14,125 --> 01:11:18,337
(AMINA AND HER GRANDFATHER TALK IN ARABIC)

965
01:11:18,379 --> 01:11:25,970
(FAINT VOICES)

966
01:11:26,012 --> 01:11:32,310
(UNINTELLIGIBLE DIALOGUE)

967
01:11:32,351 --> 01:11:35,980
(FAINT VOICES)

968
01:11:36,022 --> 01:11:38,816
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

969
01:11:38,858 --> 01:11:46,858
(UNINTELLIGIBLE DIALOGUE)

970
01:11:47,074 --> 01:11:53,080
(AMINA AND THE MAN SPEAK IN ARABIC)

971
01:11:53,122 --> 01:12:00,004
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

972
01:12:00,046 --> 01:12:04,342
(KARIN, HIS FATHER AND
THE MAN SPEAK IN ARABIC)

973
01:12:05,176 --> 01:12:08,471
(Karim) Amina! Amina!

974
01:12:08,512 --> 01:12:10,181
(AMINA CRIES OUT LOUD)

975
01:12:10,222 --> 01:12:12,016
What the fuck have you done?

976
01:12:12,058 --> 01:12:15,770
Take her. Just take her to the car.

977
01:12:15,811 --> 01:12:17,480
(Karim) Amina!

978
01:12:17,521 --> 01:12:19,523
(AMINA SCREAMS)

979
01:12:19,565 --> 01:12:23,152
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

980
01:12:23,194 --> 01:12:25,571
Be careful! Be careful!

981
01:12:25,613 --> 01:12:29,158
- Try to keep her calm. Try to keep her calm.
- Go, go, go, go!

982
01:12:29,200 --> 01:12:31,577
- (AMINA CRIES AND SCREAMS)
- Come on!

983
01:12:31,619 --> 01:12:33,621
(SOUND OF THE ENGINE THAT DOESN'T START)

984
01:12:33,662 --> 01:12:36,374
- Hey, Mara, Come on!
- It's okay. It's okay.

985
01:12:36,415 --> 01:12:39,043
Nobody's going to hurt you, okay?

986
01:12:39,085 --> 01:12:40,628
- (Mara) Amina...
- Fuck. Come on.

987
01:12:41,670 --> 01:12:43,798
(AMINA SAYS SOMETHING IN ARABIC)

988
01:12:43,839 --> 01:12:46,068
- What does that mean? Carl!
- I don't know. I don't know!

989
01:12:46,092 --> 01:12:47,843
Amina!

990
01:12:47,885 --> 01:12:49,165
(Mara) What are you doing, Carl?

991
01:12:50,471 --> 01:12:52,598
- (Mara) Carl, go!
- (Carl) Okay.

992
01:12:52,640 --> 01:12:55,184
(Carl) Come on, Come on, come on.
Damn it, come on!

993
01:12:56,018 --> 01:12:58,104
(Carl) Fuck! Here we go, here we go.

994
01:12:58,145 --> 01:13:00,481
(TIRES SCREECHING AND AMINA CRYING)

995
01:13:00,523 --> 01:13:02,316
No, no!

996
01:13:02,358 --> 01:13:05,861
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

997
01:13:07,530 --> 01:13:11,117
- No, no, no. She cannot be here.
- No, no, no, no, let us in, let us in, let us in.

998
01:13:11,158 --> 01:13:13,285
Just until we figure this mess out.

999
01:13:14,787 --> 01:13:18,666
It's all right. Does she speak English?
I don't know if she speaks English.

1000
01:13:18,707 --> 01:13:20,501
(SOUNDS OF ANGER)

1001
01:13:20,543 --> 01:13:22,002
Amina?

1002
01:13:33,848 --> 01:13:35,516
Tell her I love her.

1003
01:13:35,558 --> 01:13:38,358
(Mara) And tell her she should never
have been brought to this country.

1004
01:13:38,394 --> 01:13:41,355
And I didn't know
and I couldn't find her.

1005
01:13:41,397 --> 01:13:44,358
And I just... I just want to take her back
to America...

1006
01:13:44,400 --> 01:13:47,862
...to be her mom, to be your mom.

1007
01:13:47,903 --> 01:13:51,240
She is your mother.
She is your mother, Amina.

1008
01:13:52,575 --> 01:13:56,245
I don't have a mother.
My mother is dead.

1009
01:13:59,081 --> 01:14:00,916
What?

1010
01:14:01,792 --> 01:14:06,547
She said: "I don't have a mother.
My mother is dead".

1011
01:14:06,589 --> 01:14:14,589
(AMINA CRIES DESPERATELY)

1012
01:14:15,181 --> 01:14:18,934
(DASIA SPEAKS IN ARABIC AND AMINA CRES)

1013
01:14:18,976 --> 01:14:20,936
(Robeson) What's going on?

1014
01:14:20,978 --> 01:14:23,647
- What the fuck!
- It's not how it looks.

1015
01:14:23,689 --> 01:14:26,358
- Really?
- We had to grab her. We had no other choice.

1016
01:14:26,400 --> 01:14:28,486
(AMINA CRIES)

1017
01:14:28,527 --> 01:14:30,696
We can't stay here.

1018
01:14:30,738 --> 01:14:38,738
(DRAMATIC MUSIC)

1019
01:14:42,374 --> 01:14:44,877
- Amina. Amina, you have to come with me.
- No!

1020
01:14:44,919 --> 01:14:48,088
(DASIA SPEAKS IN ARABIC)

1021
01:14:48,130 --> 01:14:51,175
(AMINA CRIES)

1022
01:14:51,217 --> 01:14:53,093
Take this.

1023
01:14:53,135 --> 01:14:57,348
You should have known better.
It was the wrong way.

1024
01:14:57,389 --> 01:15:05,389
(DRAMATIC MUSIC)

1025
01:15:37,221 --> 01:15:41,559
(BIRDS SINGING
AND VOICES FROM THE OUTSIDE)

1026
01:15:51,610 --> 01:15:56,574
So, ehm... Carl just told me
you speak good English.

1027
01:15:59,285 --> 01:16:01,579
You're stubborn, huh?

1028
01:16:02,580 --> 01:16:05,165
I guess you got
something from me after all.

1029
01:16:07,459 --> 01:16:09,962
Maybe he's wrong.
Maybe you don't speak.

1030
01:16:11,171 --> 01:16:13,382
I'm top of my class in English.

1031
01:16:14,633 --> 01:16:17,177
You were always super smart, Mina.

1032
01:16:17,219 --> 01:16:19,054
Amina.

1033
01:16:19,096 --> 01:16:20,973
Amina, sorry.

1034
01:16:24,602 --> 01:16:29,523
Ehm... I have carried this
every day since you left.

1035
01:16:41,118 --> 01:16:42,828
Also...

1036
01:16:45,914 --> 01:16:48,167
(Mara) This is me and you.

1037
01:16:48,208 --> 01:16:50,669
(Mara) You're four, it's your birthday.

1038
01:16:52,963 --> 01:16:59,303
You're much older now.
Do you have any hobbies?

1039
01:17:01,472 --> 01:17:03,265
You still like swimming?

1040
01:17:03,307 --> 01:17:06,352
- We have a pool.
- Wow. Huh? You do?

1041
01:17:06,393 --> 01:17:09,146
I race on the team.

1042
01:17:09,188 --> 01:17:11,565
I'm... How do you say?

1043
01:17:11,607 --> 01:17:13,484
- Oh, Captain?
- Captain.

1044
01:17:13,525 --> 01:17:14,777
Wow.

1045
01:17:16,195 --> 01:17:20,240
You know, I was the one
who taught you how to swim.

1046
01:17:21,116 --> 01:17:24,745
At home, at the lake,
with your grandpa.

1047
01:17:27,206 --> 01:17:29,333
I have my "jaddy" here.

1048
01:17:29,375 --> 01:17:31,627
Your "jaddy", that's what you call?

1049
01:17:33,379 --> 01:17:34,588
Where is he?

1050
01:17:36,882 --> 01:17:40,094
Oh... He died.

1051
01:17:40,135 --> 01:17:43,389
He'd been sick for a long time...

1052
01:17:43,430 --> 01:17:47,768
...but he wanted me to tell you
that he loved you...

1053
01:17:47,810 --> 01:17:49,687
...very, very much.

1054
01:17:54,733 --> 01:17:56,044
(Robeson) You should have waited.

1055
01:17:56,068 --> 01:17:59,488
I'm done waiting, dummy.
I saw an opportunity and I took it.

1056
01:17:59,530 --> 01:18:02,241
- You're reckless.
- I'm her mother.

1057
01:18:03,575 --> 01:18:08,372
I saw her, you know?
After all this time.

1058
01:18:09,039 --> 01:18:11,917
(whining) I'd imagined it for so long.

1059
01:18:13,544 --> 01:18:17,339
(whining) My heart, Mitchell.
I couldn't wait

1060
01:18:20,259 --> 01:18:26,056
Mitchell, it's me. I imagined her
running into my harms.

1061
01:18:26,098 --> 01:18:29,935
But now she's looking at me
like I'm a fucking monster.

1062
01:18:33,480 --> 01:18:35,566
How do we get out of this country?

1063
01:18:37,526 --> 01:18:39,862
We have to take Amina back to Karim.

1064
01:18:40,946 --> 01:18:43,615
- Is that a joke?
- I can't get her out.

1065
01:18:43,657 --> 01:18:45,868
We're all in danger if we don't return her.

1066
01:18:45,909 --> 01:18:48,120
Why? What's happened?

1067
01:18:48,162 --> 01:18:49,663
You have to trust me.

1068
01:18:49,705 --> 01:18:51,582
- Oh, what? Trust you?
- Yes.

1069
01:18:51,623 --> 01:18:55,461
After I finally do the thing
that no one was prepared to help me with...

1070
01:18:55,502 --> 01:18:57,212
...you're telling me to take her back?

1071
01:18:57,254 --> 01:18:59,548
What the fuck is going on?

1072
01:18:59,590 --> 01:19:04,386
If you try to get past me, I will kill you. If
you play one finger on her, I will fuck you up.

1073
01:19:04,428 --> 01:19:07,931
- Stop! Stop!
- Tell me what's going... Tell me!

1074
01:19:07,973 --> 01:19:11,727
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

1075
01:19:11,769 --> 01:19:13,979
Karim has ties to Muslim Brotherhood.

1076
01:19:14,021 --> 01:19:15,856
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

1077
01:19:15,898 --> 01:19:18,108
(Robeson) There, now you know.

1078
01:19:18,150 --> 01:19:19,777
What?

1079
01:19:21,069 --> 01:19:23,572
Apparently, he got caught up
to his family's connections.

1080
01:19:23,614 --> 01:19:26,158
They blackmailed him
into laundering money for them.

1081
01:19:26,575 --> 01:19:28,994
And that's when the CIA discovered him.

1082
01:19:29,703 --> 01:19:31,830
Oh, the CIA knew?

1083
01:19:31,872 --> 01:19:36,168
Mara, we're hired contractors.

1084
01:19:36,210 --> 01:19:41,548
My contact, Louis, told me Karim
cut a deal with the CIA as an informant.

1085
01:19:42,716 --> 01:19:44,593
He works for them.

1086
01:19:46,678 --> 01:19:49,056
In return, he gets to keep Amina.

1087
01:19:50,224 --> 01:19:52,893
(Robeson) He's been
relocating them out here.

1088
01:19:52,935 --> 01:19:55,479
(Robeson) Sorry. I just found this out.

1089
01:19:57,481 --> 01:19:59,775
All those dead ends.

1090
01:20:01,693 --> 01:20:06,323
He blocked my search in Washington,
and hired you to keep me from her.

1091
01:20:08,742 --> 01:20:10,285
Yes.

1092
01:20:12,871 --> 01:20:15,082
Okay. Muslim Brotherhood.

1093
01:20:16,917 --> 01:20:19,044
I thought he was having affairs.

1094
01:20:20,462 --> 01:20:23,173
If we don't get you out
and return her...

1095
01:20:25,551 --> 01:20:28,053
...I honestly don't know what he might do.

1096
01:20:28,095 --> 01:20:32,474
(Mara, crying out loud) Oh! Oh!

1097
01:20:32,516 --> 01:20:35,143
- Please, stop...
- (Mara) OH!

1098
01:20:35,185 --> 01:20:37,855
You kept me working for you.

1099
01:20:37,896 --> 01:20:40,732
You slept with me.

1100
01:20:41,066 --> 01:20:43,151
I'm sorry, okay?

1101
01:20:43,193 --> 01:20:50,158
(DRAMATIC MUSIC)

1102
01:20:50,200 --> 01:20:53,245
So what are you going to do now, Mitch?

1103
01:20:53,287 --> 01:20:57,124
Because I am not giving her back.
And we both know it.

1104
01:20:58,333 --> 01:21:01,837
So either help me or let me go.

1105
01:21:01,879 --> 01:21:09,879
(DRAMATIC MUSIC)

1106
01:21:10,095 --> 01:21:13,140
When this is over,
I never want to hear from you again.

1107
01:21:13,181 --> 01:21:17,978
(DRAMATIC MUSIC)

1108
01:21:18,020 --> 01:21:20,397
(AMINA SIGHS)

1109
01:21:22,983 --> 01:21:24,651
You're ready?

1110
01:21:26,278 --> 01:21:30,240
(BARKING OF A DOG)

1111
01:21:32,910 --> 01:21:39,082
(BARKING DOGS)

1112
01:21:39,124 --> 01:21:41,668
Here. Keep your faces covered.

1113
01:21:45,130 --> 01:21:53,130
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

1114
01:21:55,682 --> 01:21:57,976
(FAINT NOISES)

1115
01:21:59,728 --> 01:22:01,146
(Mara) Where are we?

1116
01:22:01,188 --> 01:22:04,024
We need to stop for papers
so we can get across the border.

1117
01:22:04,066 --> 01:22:07,027
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

1118
01:22:07,069 --> 01:22:11,657
Thanks for being so quick. I owe
you. I'll call you when I get to Damascus.

1119
01:22:11,698 --> 01:22:19,456
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

1120
01:22:19,498 --> 01:22:21,458
(Amina) Is he your husband?

1121
01:22:22,417 --> 01:22:23,835
No.

1122
01:22:24,711 --> 01:22:26,880
Would he be with us in America?

1123
01:22:27,255 --> 01:22:30,467
No, we just...
We just work together, that's all.

1124
01:22:32,010 --> 01:22:34,554
(Mara) Hey, do you want a swing?

1125
01:22:38,141 --> 01:22:39,851
(Mara) Come on.

1126
01:22:44,314 --> 01:22:46,316
It's okay. You on?

1127
01:22:47,192 --> 01:22:49,486
- Mm-mm.
- All right, I got you.

1128
01:22:50,278 --> 01:22:55,325
Okay. Are you ready? One, two, three.

1129
01:22:55,367 --> 01:23:03,367
(CHEERFUL MUSIC)

1130
01:23:05,836 --> 01:23:07,921
(MARA LAUGHS)

1131
01:23:07,963 --> 01:23:11,299
(CHEERFUL MUSIC)

1132
01:23:11,341 --> 01:23:14,386
(MARA AND AMINA LAUGH)

1133
01:23:14,428 --> 01:23:18,140
(CHEERFUL MUSIC)

1134
01:23:18,181 --> 01:23:22,102
(JOE AND AMINA LAUGH)

1135
01:23:22,144 --> 01:23:26,523
(AMINA LAUGH)

1136
01:23:26,565 --> 01:23:28,984
(CHEERFUL MUSIC)

1137
01:23:29,026 --> 01:23:33,447
(MARA AND AMINA LAUGH)

1138
01:23:33,488 --> 01:23:41,488
(CHEERFUL MUSIC)

1139
01:23:56,344 --> 01:23:58,513
I have something similar.

1140
01:23:58,555 --> 01:24:06,555
(CHEERFUL MUSIC)

1141
01:24:08,982 --> 01:24:16,740
(UNINTELLIGIBLE DIALOGUES IN ARABIC)

1142
01:24:16,782 --> 01:24:20,911
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

1143
01:24:27,584 --> 01:24:29,544
Passport.

1144
01:24:29,586 --> 01:24:37,586
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

1145
01:24:57,656 --> 01:24:59,908
(BANGS)

1146
01:24:59,950 --> 01:25:07,950
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

1147
01:25:08,166 --> 01:25:10,293
There are Americans here.

1148
01:25:11,002 --> 01:25:13,421
They want to see your papers.

1149
01:25:13,463 --> 01:25:18,093
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

1150
01:25:18,135 --> 01:25:19,970
Shit.

1151
01:25:20,554 --> 01:25:22,097
Fuck.

1152
01:25:22,139 --> 01:25:30,139
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

1153
01:25:33,483 --> 01:25:35,068
(Amina) What is happening?

1154
01:25:35,110 --> 01:25:38,321
- We can find another route.
- It will be like this everywhere.

1155
01:25:38,363 --> 01:25:40,824
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

1156
01:25:40,866 --> 01:25:42,909
(Border guard) Going somewhere?

1157
01:25:42,951 --> 01:25:44,703
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

1158
01:25:44,744 --> 01:25:46,788
(Border guard) Go, go. "Yalla"!

1159
01:25:48,123 --> 01:25:49,916
(Border guard) Are you American?

1160
01:25:51,293 --> 01:25:53,420
(Border guard) Are you
traveling with anyone?

1161
01:25:54,171 --> 01:25:56,423
Wait. Damn, what are you doing?

1162
01:25:56,464 --> 01:25:59,759
What's best for us, Mitch.
It's okay, come on, sweetie.

1163
01:26:00,468 --> 01:26:02,179
Mara...

1164
01:26:02,220 --> 01:26:06,516
Say whatever you need to say
to keep us safe. I'm not losing her again.

1165
01:26:06,933 --> 01:26:08,768
- Hey!
- Go, Amina.

1166
01:26:09,269 --> 01:26:12,606
(FIGHTING SOUNDS AND SUSPENSE MUSIC)

1167
01:26:12,647 --> 01:26:15,692
(GUNSHOT AND FIGHTING SOUNDS)

1168
01:26:15,734 --> 01:26:17,569
Don't move!

1169
01:26:18,320 --> 01:26:20,822
Put the gun down!
Put the gun down!

1170
01:26:20,864 --> 01:26:23,783
(SOUNDS OF PAIN)

1171
01:26:23,825 --> 01:26:27,537
Go! Go when you have the chance! Go!

1172
01:26:27,579 --> 01:26:30,332
(FIGHTING SOUNDS)

1173
01:26:30,373 --> 01:26:38,373
(SUSPENSE MUSIC)

1174
01:26:43,011 --> 01:26:44,554
(Amina) Where are we going now?

1175
01:26:44,971 --> 01:26:47,933
I'm going to find us somewhere to cross.
It will be okay.

1176
01:26:48,767 --> 01:26:50,977
I'm hungry.

1177
01:26:53,438 --> 01:26:55,023
Here.

1178
01:26:55,065 --> 01:26:56,775
I only eat vegetables.

1179
01:26:57,734 --> 01:26:59,903
I don't have anything else.

1180
01:27:01,112 --> 01:27:04,241
- I want to go home now.
- I told you.

1181
01:27:04,824 --> 01:27:06,409
We are going home.

1182
01:27:07,369 --> 01:27:09,120
Not to America.

1183
01:27:11,373 --> 01:27:14,668
I like it here.
I like my friends and my house.

1184
01:27:17,170 --> 01:27:18,964
Listen.

1185
01:27:19,005 --> 01:27:22,050
You're going to make
so many new friends in America.

1186
01:27:22,842 --> 01:27:24,678
"Jaddy" won't be there.

1187
01:27:25,512 --> 01:27:28,098
- Well, no...
- (Amina) Who will be?

1188
01:27:30,976 --> 01:27:33,520
Me, Mina.

1189
01:27:36,064 --> 01:27:37,774
Amina.

1190
01:27:38,775 --> 01:27:40,360
(whining) Amina.

1191
01:27:40,777 --> 01:27:42,779
You and me.

1192
01:27:43,363 --> 01:27:45,490
I don't want to be with you.

1193
01:27:47,826 --> 01:27:50,245
Okay, well, you don't mean that.

1194
01:27:50,287 --> 01:27:52,640
I want to stay with baba.
Why would you take me away from him?

1195
01:27:52,664 --> 01:27:54,666
Hey! Sit down.

1196
01:27:56,209 --> 01:28:00,088
Sorry. I didn't mean
to hurt you. Are you okay?

1197
01:28:02,799 --> 01:28:04,592
It's just...

1198
01:28:06,970 --> 01:28:10,056
(crying) You don't know
how hard it's been.

1199
01:28:10,098 --> 01:28:12,225
And...

1200
01:28:12,267 --> 01:28:15,478
...how long it has taken me to find you.

1201
01:28:18,273 --> 01:28:20,650
But I was never lost.

1202
01:28:24,112 --> 01:28:25,905
What?

1203
01:28:28,116 --> 01:28:30,702
I was just at home.

1204
01:28:35,332 --> 01:28:37,959
I never asked you
to come and find me.

1205
01:28:38,001 --> 01:28:46,001
(SAD MUSIC)

1206
01:29:18,541 --> 01:29:22,712
- (Amina) Where are you going?
- (Mara) It's okay, I'm just... Wait there.

1207
01:29:22,754 --> 01:29:29,719
(SAD MUSIC)

1208
01:29:29,761 --> 01:29:35,767
(WHISTLING WIND)

1209
01:29:35,809 --> 01:29:38,144
(SOUND OF THE COUCH STOPPING)

1210
01:29:38,186 --> 01:29:46,186
(SAD MUSIC)

1211
01:29:54,411 --> 01:30:02,411
(WHISTLING WIND)

1212
01:30:28,695 --> 01:30:33,324
(WHISTLING WIND)

1213
01:30:42,375 --> 01:30:43,710
Where is she?

1214
01:30:46,045 --> 01:30:47,422
She's safe.

1215
01:30:47,464 --> 01:30:49,215
- Who's she with?
- A friend.

1216
01:30:49,257 --> 01:30:52,427
- I need to see her. Now.
- Yeah, it hurts, doesn't it?

1217
01:30:53,219 --> 01:30:55,138
Eight years of hurt.

1218
01:30:55,180 --> 01:30:57,348
- How could you do it?
- (Karim) I'm sorry.

1219
01:30:58,099 --> 01:30:59,893
I'm sorry.

1220
01:31:01,978 --> 01:31:04,564
I'm sorry for what I've
done to you, everything.

1221
01:31:04,606 --> 01:31:07,150
I swear, Mara. I was... I was cornered.

1222
01:31:07,192 --> 01:31:10,028
(Karim) If I stayed, I would have put
both of you in danger.

1223
01:31:10,069 --> 01:31:13,156
And now she's been protected
by a very powerful organization.

1224
01:31:13,198 --> 01:31:18,453
Yeah. Who helped you to kidnap her.
Do you understand how crazy that sounds?

1225
01:31:18,495 --> 01:31:22,165
The people I work for threatened me
and the family if I didn't relocate...

1226
01:31:22,207 --> 01:31:23,958
...I couldn't face it without her.

1227
01:31:24,000 --> 01:31:26,336
And honestly, I wanted
to give her a better life.

1228
01:31:26,377 --> 01:31:30,215
As long as I kept quiet and played
by the rules, they gave us that.

1229
01:31:30,256 --> 01:31:33,009
You stole her from me.

1230
01:31:35,345 --> 01:31:37,514
My little girl.

1231
01:31:39,224 --> 01:31:40,767
Our little girl.

1232
01:31:40,808 --> 01:31:42,352
(GUNSHOT)

1233
01:31:44,270 --> 01:31:46,564
Don't you fucking come near me.

1234
01:31:46,606 --> 01:31:49,776
(WHISTLING WIND)

1235
01:31:49,817 --> 01:31:52,195
Sorry. Okay?

1236
01:31:57,033 --> 01:31:58,952
(SOUNDS OF FEAR)

1237
01:31:58,993 --> 01:32:01,746
(KARIM SNIFFS)

1238
01:32:03,790 --> 01:32:06,668
(MARA EXHALES)

1239
01:32:06,709 --> 01:32:12,840
(MARA GASPS FOR BREATH)

1240
01:32:16,719 --> 01:32:19,055
Did you know I was looking for you?

1241
01:32:19,097 --> 01:32:23,184
They kept telling me
you were getting on with your life.

1242
01:32:24,394 --> 01:32:26,479
And you believed that?

1243
01:32:27,105 --> 01:32:29,023
It was easier that way.

1244
01:32:29,691 --> 01:32:31,776
You took my most...

1245
01:32:32,277 --> 01:32:35,196
...precious thing I've ever had.

1246
01:32:35,989 --> 01:32:38,825
(crying) You obliterated my life.

1247
01:32:38,866 --> 01:32:42,620
And you spent this whole time
telling her that I was dead.

1248
01:32:43,496 --> 01:32:47,333
I don't... I don't get
how you can hate me that much.

1249
01:32:47,375 --> 01:32:50,086
- I don't. I don't hate you. I thought...
- (Mara) Shut up!

1250
01:32:50,128 --> 01:32:52,839
I don't give a fuck of
what you think, Karim.

1251
01:32:52,880 --> 01:32:56,676
I swear to God, if you say
another fucking word, I will kill you.

1252
01:32:57,594 --> 01:32:59,721
(Mara) You have no idea.

1253
01:32:59,762 --> 01:33:02,223
(WHISTLING WIND)

1254
01:33:02,265 --> 01:33:04,934
(SAD MUSIC)

1255
01:33:08,438 --> 01:33:12,150
But she's not the little
girl that I lost anymore.

1256
01:33:12,191 --> 01:33:14,986
(SAD MUSIC)

1257
01:33:15,028 --> 01:33:17,447
(crying) She doesn't know me.

1258
01:33:17,488 --> 01:33:20,074
(SAD MUSIC)

1259
01:33:20,116 --> 01:33:22,035
So I guess...

1260
01:33:23,244 --> 01:33:26,664
...I kind of am dead, aren't I?

1261
01:33:27,206 --> 01:33:29,042
Thanks to you.

1262
01:33:29,083 --> 01:33:33,921
(WHISTLING WIND)

1263
01:33:33,963 --> 01:33:40,261
(MARA CRIES SILENTLY AND DESPERATELY)

1264
01:33:40,303 --> 01:33:43,014
Promise me she'll be safe with you.

1265
01:33:43,056 --> 01:33:47,352
(SAD MUSIC)

1266
01:33:47,393 --> 01:33:49,187
Promise me!

1267
01:33:50,521 --> 01:33:52,398
I promise.

1268
01:33:52,440 --> 01:33:54,067
She's safe.

1269
01:33:54,108 --> 01:33:56,944
She's happy.
She has a good life here.

1270
01:33:56,986 --> 01:33:58,780
(Karim) You're seeing it for yourself.

1271
01:33:58,821 --> 01:34:02,492
(crying) Was it ever real? You and me?

1272
01:34:05,828 --> 01:34:09,082
Yes. I loved you, Mara.

1273
01:34:09,123 --> 01:34:11,125
(Karim, whining) I did.

1274
01:34:11,167 --> 01:34:12,919
(MARA SIGHS)

1275
01:34:15,505 --> 01:34:18,716
All right, so you're going
to tell Amina the truth.

1276
01:34:18,758 --> 01:34:21,094
(Mara) You're going to tell her
that it was your fault...

1277
01:34:21,135 --> 01:34:24,347
...if she hasn't had a mother
to be there for her this whole time.

1278
01:34:25,139 --> 01:34:29,018
You're going to tell her everything
that I did to try to find her.

1279
01:34:29,060 --> 01:34:31,270
(Mara) You're going to
beg for her forgiveness...

1280
01:34:31,312 --> 01:34:34,857
...and then you're going to help us
rebuild our lives together, okay?

1281
01:34:37,902 --> 01:34:39,654
(KARIM SNIFFS)

1282
01:34:39,696 --> 01:34:41,447
I will.

1283
01:34:42,073 --> 01:34:44,117
This is not for you.

1284
01:34:44,826 --> 01:34:46,327
This is for her.

1285
01:35:00,133 --> 01:35:02,802
I understand what my daughter needs.

1286
01:35:05,847 --> 01:35:07,974
I always have.

1287
01:35:10,518 --> 01:35:14,397
(KARIM GASPS FOR BREATH)

1288
01:35:14,439 --> 01:35:22,071
(SAD MUSIC)

1289
01:35:22,113 --> 01:35:24,824
Amina, it's okay, I promise.

1290
01:35:24,866 --> 01:35:31,998
(SAD MUSIC)

1291
01:35:32,039 --> 01:35:33,791
Hey.

1292
01:35:33,833 --> 01:35:41,507
(SAD MUSIC)

1293
01:35:41,549 --> 01:35:43,384
Remember:...

1294
01:35:44,177 --> 01:35:46,262
...I've always loved you.

1295
01:35:46,304 --> 01:35:54,304
(SAD MUSIC)

1296
01:35:55,480 --> 01:35:57,982
(KARIM LAUGHS)

1297
01:35:58,024 --> 01:36:00,568
- (Karim) Amina!
- (Amina) Baba!

1298
01:36:00,610 --> 01:36:07,116
(SAD MUSIC)

1299
01:36:07,158 --> 01:36:13,998
(AMINA AND KARIM CRY)

1300
01:36:14,040 --> 01:36:18,544
(SAD MUSIC)

1301
01:36:18,586 --> 01:36:20,254
(KARIM SNIFFS)

1302
01:36:20,296 --> 01:36:28,296
(SAD MUSIC)

1303
01:36:33,184 --> 01:36:35,478
(SMACK OF A KISS)

1304
01:36:35,520 --> 01:36:40,149
(SAD MUSIC)

1305
01:36:40,191 --> 01:36:44,987
(MARA CRIES)

1306
01:36:45,029 --> 01:36:47,031
(SAD MUSIC)

